WEBVTT

00:00.008 --> 00:35.166
Support Admin Watch on
kissasia.cam or kisskh.org

00:03.794 --> 00:06.071
<i> (static crackling softly)</i>

00:42.371 --> 00:45.275
<i> (rotary telephone dialing)</i>

00:56.680 --> 00:59.014
(wind whistling softly)

01:04.597 --> 01:06.395
Hello?

01:08.328 --> 01:10.293
Hope. Hope Adler.

01:10.428 --> 01:12.236
Who is this?

01:15.400 --> 01:17.703
Alpine Lake.

01:17.838 --> 01:21.080
It-it's a youth camp
in the mountains.

01:26.751 --> 01:28.516
I, um...

01:30.516 --> 01:32.619
I had these dreams.

01:33.551 --> 01:35.786
Seven numbers.

01:35.921 --> 01:38.559
No area code,
so this call is local.

01:39.494 --> 01:41.760
You're here in Colorado, right?

01:45.906 --> 01:48.602
The numbers were carved in ice.

01:50.269 --> 01:51.638
Yes.

01:52.546 --> 01:53.904
Yes!

01:56.573 --> 01:58.781
Who is this?

01:58.916 --> 02:00.779
Who are you?

02:03.047 --> 02:05.316
-Hello?
-(static droning over phone)

02:05.452 --> 02:07.918
Hello? Can you hear me?

02:09.255 --> 02:10.524
Hello?

02:10.659 --> 02:12.296
-(high-pitched tone over phone)
-(gasps)

02:16.561 --> 02:19.204
(breath trembling)

02:32.785 --> 02:35.616
♪ ♪

02:58.239 --> 03:01.037
♪ ♪

03:26.531 --> 03:29.032
♪ ♪

03:40.420 --> 03:41.911
STUDENTS (chanting):
<i> Fight! Fight!</i>

03:42.047 --> 03:43.920
Fight! Fight!
Fight! Fight! Fight!

03:44.056 --> 03:45.350
Fight! Fight! Fight!

03:45.486 --> 03:47.721
(students clamoring)

03:48.854 --> 03:51.087
(students groaning, laughing)

03:53.063 --> 03:54.098
(groaning)

03:54.234 --> 03:55.564
STUDENT:
Got to get up, man.

03:57.003 --> 03:58.361
GWEN:
Finn!

03:58.496 --> 03:59.599
Finn!

03:59.735 --> 04:01.000
STUDENT:
You're hurting him!

04:01.136 --> 04:02.770
Finney!

04:02.906 --> 04:04.841
STUDENT ON GROUND (panting):
Please, stop. Please.

04:04.977 --> 04:06.674
You done yet?

04:08.041 --> 04:09.574
-(students groan)
-STUDENT ON GROUND: Yes.

04:09.709 --> 04:10.909
Stay the fuck away from me.

04:12.748 --> 04:14.550
-(Finn grunts)
-(students groaning)

04:18.517 --> 04:20.255
Anyone else?

04:20.390 --> 04:22.657
(students murmuring quietly)

04:30.200 --> 04:32.029
GWEN:
Hey.

04:33.468 --> 04:35.298
What the hell was that?

04:35.434 --> 04:36.768
New kid.

04:36.904 --> 04:38.237
Are you just beating up
new kids now?

04:38.373 --> 04:39.471
He started it.

04:39.606 --> 04:41.570
What was it this time?

04:41.706 --> 04:43.372
Uh, the usual.

04:43.508 --> 04:45.984
"Heard you were the badass
that wasted a serial killer.

04:46.120 --> 04:47.282
You don't look so tough."

04:47.418 --> 04:48.645
He didn't really say that.

04:48.780 --> 04:51.552
Yeah, he actually did.

04:51.687 --> 04:53.848
Did you have to go
so hard on him?

04:53.984 --> 04:56.460
In a situation like that,

04:56.595 --> 04:59.754
the more blood, the better--
for the crowd.

04:59.890 --> 05:01.299
Proves a stronger point.

05:01.435 --> 05:02.961
You've made that point
more than once,

05:03.096 --> 05:05.534
so maybe--
and I'm just spitballing here--

05:05.670 --> 05:07.662
maybe the point
you're actually making

05:07.798 --> 05:10.133
is less "don't fuck with me"
and more "I'm the guy to beat."

05:11.372 --> 05:13.042
Hey, Gwen, Finn.

05:13.177 --> 05:14.570
Great fight, man.

05:14.705 --> 05:16.006
Thanks, Ernesto.

05:16.142 --> 05:17.745
-Hi, Ernie.
-ERNESTO: So, uh, tonight,

05:17.881 --> 05:19.514
uh, I'm going to go down
to the Civic Center

05:19.650 --> 05:21.617
to wait in line
for Duran Duran tickets.

05:21.752 --> 05:23.955
-Duran Duran tickets?
-He just said that.

05:24.091 --> 05:26.155
Simon Le Bon is so choice.

05:26.290 --> 05:28.853
A-Are you going, Gwen?

05:28.988 --> 05:31.296
I wish.
Those tickets cost a mint.

05:31.432 --> 05:33.459
My treat.
I was gonna buy two anyway.

05:33.595 --> 05:35.393
It'd, you know, be cool

05:35.528 --> 05:37.501
to have someone to go with
who's... who's also a fan.

05:38.435 --> 05:39.795
-For real?
-For real.

05:39.931 --> 05:40.971
That'd be radical.

05:41.106 --> 05:42.506
Consider it done.

05:44.039 --> 05:46.105
All right, well,
I-I got to get to shop class.

05:46.241 --> 05:47.174
See ya.

05:47.309 --> 05:49.447
(car departing)

05:50.579 --> 05:52.217
You know that's a date.

05:52.353 --> 05:55.153
-No, it's not.
-Yeah, it is.

05:55.288 --> 05:57.554
Okay, so what if it's a date?

05:59.187 --> 06:02.355
I don't know, I...
I just don't like him.

06:02.490 --> 06:03.995
I don't get why.

06:04.130 --> 06:05.562
He's really nice.

06:05.697 --> 06:07.356
Besides that,
don't you think Robin

06:07.491 --> 06:09.361
would want you looking out
for his kid brother?

06:09.496 --> 06:11.963
But that doesn't mean letting
him boink my little sister.

06:12.099 --> 06:13.570
-Ow.
-Don't be gross, jizz mopper.

06:13.705 --> 06:15.770
<i> ("Subways of Your Mind"</i>
<i> by FEX playing)</i>

06:15.906 --> 06:17.207
ANNOUNCER:
Welcome back to<i> Night Flight.</i>

06:17.342 --> 06:19.004
Here's German band FEX

06:19.139 --> 06:21.505
with their new hit,
"Subways of Your Mind."

06:21.640 --> 06:23.745
♪ ♪

06:27.349 --> 06:28.381
Night, Son.

06:28.516 --> 06:30.579
I'm off to bed.

06:30.714 --> 06:32.386
Night.

06:32.522 --> 06:34.551
Don't stay up too late.

06:34.686 --> 06:36.989
Yeah, sure.

06:37.124 --> 06:41.697
♪ Take the consequence
of living ♪

06:44.469 --> 06:45.767
♪ There's no space ♪

06:48.198 --> 06:51.773
♪ There's no tomorrow ♪

06:51.908 --> 06:57.545
♪ There's no sense,
communication ♪

06:57.681 --> 06:59.517
♪ Check it in, check it out ♪

06:59.652 --> 07:04.080
♪ But the sun
will never shine... ♪

07:04.216 --> 07:06.755
-(door creaks)
-(crickets chirping)

07:11.994 --> 07:14.961
-(wind gusting)
-(dog barking in distance)

07:33.918 --> 07:36.653
If you try to touch me,
I'll scratch your face.

07:41.955 --> 07:43.759
THE GRABBER:
This face?

07:55.337 --> 07:57.003
Hey.

08:04.910 --> 08:06.177
Still not my thing.

08:07.417 --> 08:08.349
Don't tell Dad.

08:08.485 --> 08:09.955
Fuck off, slap-dick.

08:10.090 --> 08:11.116
I'm no narc.

08:13.917 --> 08:16.389
You okay?

08:16.525 --> 08:17.925
I'm fine.

08:19.296 --> 08:20.991
No, I-I mean...

08:21.126 --> 08:22.897
I don't want to talk about it.

08:28.366 --> 08:30.509
It's okay
that you feel this way.

08:32.236 --> 08:34.403
You don't know how I feel.

08:36.445 --> 08:37.912
No, but...

08:39.147 --> 08:42.477
I know, however you feel,
it's okay.

08:48.953 --> 08:51.259
(static crackles)

08:51.394 --> 08:53.389
♪ ♪

09:11.678 --> 09:13.882
♪ ♪

09:19.885 --> 09:21.956
(static crackling)

09:23.327 --> 09:25.520
♪ ♪

09:38.672 --> 09:40.711
♪ ♪

09:49.882 --> 09:51.121
(static crackles)

09:51.256 --> 09:53.449
♪ ♪

10:13.278 --> 10:15.471
♪ ♪

10:19.451 --> 10:21.317
(phone ringing loudly)

10:21.452 --> 10:23.587
(breath trembling)

10:23.723 --> 10:26.515
(phone continues ringing
in distance)

10:36.095 --> 10:38.934
(phone continues ringing)

10:53.453 --> 10:56.116
(phone continues ringing)

10:59.492 --> 11:02.452
(ringing continues in distance)

11:11.438 --> 11:13.672
(phone continues ringing)

11:17.404 --> 11:20.470
(ringing continues faintly
in distance)

11:24.751 --> 11:26.245
FINN (muffled):
Hey, what are you doing?

11:27.813 --> 11:29.347
Hey.

11:31.147 --> 11:32.790
Hey, Gwen.

11:34.520 --> 11:36.722
(clearly):
Gwen, wake up. What are you...

11:36.858 --> 11:38.730
Why are you so cold?

11:40.166 --> 11:41.832
Finn?

11:43.501 --> 11:44.831
It's okay.

11:44.966 --> 11:46.298
You were sleepwalking again.

11:48.036 --> 11:51.006
Jesus. Your skin is like ice.

11:52.301 --> 11:54.405
I had a bad dream.

11:55.940 --> 11:57.682
(sighs)

11:57.817 --> 12:00.913
It's okay.
Just... go back to bed.

12:01.048 --> 12:02.917
I-I said I had a bad dream.

12:03.053 --> 12:05.548
I heard you.
Just go back to bed.

12:06.525 --> 12:08.760
(school bell ringing)

12:14.091 --> 12:15.767
Hey, witch.

12:19.166 --> 12:21.102
(students chattering quietly)

12:22.066 --> 12:24.435
(laughter)

12:25.872 --> 12:27.174
Hey, Gwen.

12:28.105 --> 12:29.942
Hey, Ernie.

12:30.078 --> 12:31.844
ERNESTO:
Check it out.

12:31.980 --> 12:33.109
GWEN:
Oh, choice.

12:33.245 --> 12:34.951
I can't believe it.

12:36.153 --> 12:38.488
So, uh, you're into
a lot of that...

12:38.624 --> 12:41.018
that woo-woo stuff, right?

12:41.153 --> 12:43.387
What? You mean ghosts?

12:43.523 --> 12:45.764
Spirits?
Glimpses of the world beyond?

12:47.666 --> 12:49.393
-Yeah.
-Okay, then.

12:49.529 --> 12:52.496
Yeah, I believe in
all that woo-woo stuff.

12:55.131 --> 12:56.874
Cool.

12:57.943 --> 13:00.603
Uh, I-I brought you
something else.

13:01.944 --> 13:04.115
Ernesto, is this<i> lotería?</i>

13:04.250 --> 13:05.574
Yeah.

13:05.710 --> 13:07.452
My<i> abuela</i> sells them
in her shop,

13:07.587 --> 13:09.117
and I thought they looked cool.

13:10.117 --> 13:11.248
They're like tarot.

13:11.383 --> 13:12.789
GWEN:
These are beautiful.

13:12.925 --> 13:14.815
I mean, you can use them
like tarot.

13:14.951 --> 13:18.253
If you have the sight,
they can show you things.

13:18.389 --> 13:21.232
And you have that, right?

13:21.367 --> 13:23.023
Have what?

13:23.159 --> 13:25.659
Oh, I mean, like, you have...
you have dreams and stuff,

13:25.795 --> 13:28.169
and they...
they show you things?

13:30.334 --> 13:32.470
Where did you hear that?

13:33.940 --> 13:36.177
My parents.

13:36.312 --> 13:38.108
Back, you know,
they said that the police got

13:38.244 --> 13:40.783
an anonymous call where...

13:40.918 --> 13:43.745
where, um, Robin's body was.

13:44.656 --> 13:46.621
But they say it was you.

13:46.757 --> 13:49.854
That you dreamed it.

13:49.989 --> 13:51.794
Or-or something.

13:51.929 --> 13:54.195
I don't like talking about that.

13:55.434 --> 13:57.799
Mm, why not?

13:57.934 --> 14:00.271
'Cause it's weird.

14:00.407 --> 14:01.433
I'm weird.

14:02.641 --> 14:05.338
Maybe I like weird.

14:12.277 --> 14:14.446
(entry bell jingling)

14:17.522 --> 14:20.221
(phone ringing)

14:31.134 --> 14:33.102
I'm sorry, but I can't help you.

14:41.371 --> 14:43.039
(static crackles)

14:43.174 --> 14:45.807
♪ ♪

14:56.924 --> 14:59.062
♪ ♪

15:01.325 --> 15:03.561
(static crackling)

15:06.505 --> 15:08.698
♪ ♪

15:19.210 --> 15:21.249
♪ ♪

15:35.930 --> 15:38.134
♪ ♪

15:52.947 --> 15:55.151
♪ ♪

16:08.261 --> 16:09.194
(phone ringing loudly)

16:09.329 --> 16:11.299
(phone ringing in distance)

16:16.971 --> 16:18.603
(ringing stops)

16:23.307 --> 16:25.511
♪ ♪

16:40.324 --> 16:42.528
♪ ♪

16:58.477 --> 17:00.513
(phone ringing in distance)

17:09.554 --> 17:11.689
(phone continues ringing)

17:20.433 --> 17:22.799
(phone continues ringing)

17:25.745 --> 17:28.244
(ringing grows louder)

17:37.549 --> 17:40.289
(phone continues ringing)

17:50.834 --> 17:52.565
(ringing stops)

17:54.199 --> 17:55.799
Hello?

17:56.899 --> 17:59.071
HOPE (over phone):
Hello?

17:59.206 --> 18:01.469
Who's this?

18:01.604 --> 18:03.343
Hope. Hope Adler.

18:03.479 --> 18:06.176
-Who is this?
-(breath trembling)

18:06.311 --> 18:08.445
My name is Gwen.

18:08.580 --> 18:11.089
Where are you calling from?

18:12.757 --> 18:14.125
Alpine Lake.

18:14.260 --> 18:17.487
It-it's a youth camp
in the mountains.

18:17.622 --> 18:20.193
How did you get this number?

18:20.328 --> 18:24.062
I, um... I had these dreams.

18:24.198 --> 18:26.202
Seven numbers.

18:26.337 --> 18:28.939
No area code,
so this call is local.

18:29.074 --> 18:30.902
You're here in Colorado, right?

18:31.038 --> 18:32.066
Yes.

18:34.738 --> 18:37.447
The numbers were carved in ice.

18:37.583 --> 18:38.912
By boys.

18:39.047 --> 18:40.584
Underwater.

18:40.719 --> 18:42.583
Yes. Yes!

18:42.719 --> 18:46.322
I had the same dreams,
but the boys carved letters.

18:47.451 --> 18:49.527
Who is this?

18:49.662 --> 18:51.262
Who are you?

18:51.397 --> 18:53.156
-My name is Gwen.
-(static crackling over phone)

18:53.291 --> 18:54.930
Hello?

18:55.066 --> 18:56.894
I-I said my name is Gwen.

18:57.029 --> 18:59.166
(breaking up under static):
Hello? Can you hear me?

18:59.301 --> 19:00.761
(static droning over phone)

19:00.896 --> 19:02.998
(line clicks, static stops)

19:07.945 --> 19:10.148
(gasping breaths)

19:11.280 --> 19:13.349
You shouldn't be here.

19:14.952 --> 19:16.979
(door clanks)

19:20.454 --> 19:22.820
(door clanks, creaks open)

19:25.726 --> 19:28.595
(footsteps slowly
descending stairs)

19:35.466 --> 19:37.265
(phone ringing)

19:37.401 --> 19:39.705
-(footsteps continue)
-(Gwen's breath trembling)

19:41.577 --> 19:44.208
-(footsteps approaching)
-FINN: Hey.

19:44.343 --> 19:45.813
Hey, Gwen.

19:45.948 --> 19:46.976
Gwen.

19:52.682 --> 19:54.186
Am I really here?

19:54.321 --> 19:56.625
You're okay.

19:56.761 --> 19:59.559
You were sleepwalking again.
You came here in your sleep.

19:59.695 --> 20:01.727
I heard you leave,
and I followed you.

20:04.128 --> 20:06.435
I feel like I'm crazy.
What the hell?

20:06.570 --> 20:08.328
-Hey, hey. Look at me. Hey, hey.
-What the hell?!

20:08.464 --> 20:10.538
You're okay,
you're okay, you're okay.

20:13.836 --> 20:15.576
I-I was on the phone.

20:17.881 --> 20:18.909
Finn.

20:21.019 --> 20:22.847
I was talking to Mom.

20:26.684 --> 20:27.922
It was just a dream.

20:28.057 --> 20:29.927
N-No, it was...

20:30.063 --> 20:33.092
a dream, yeah, but it was her.

20:33.228 --> 20:35.095
She called me.

20:35.230 --> 20:37.228
From a youth camp.

20:37.364 --> 20:39.270
A youth camp?

20:40.967 --> 20:43.538
She reached out to me
from there for a reason.

20:45.377 --> 20:48.103
Come on.
Let's get you out of here.

21:07.931 --> 21:09.564
(spits)

21:17.167 --> 21:19.668
-What's this?
-Camp Alpine Lake.

21:19.804 --> 21:22.274
The camp Mom called from.

21:22.410 --> 21:23.439
We have to go there.

21:23.574 --> 21:26.377
Gwen, stop this.

21:26.513 --> 21:28.544
It was just a dream.

21:28.680 --> 21:30.146
About a real place.

21:30.281 --> 21:32.223
A place I found.
It's why I had the dream.

21:32.358 --> 21:33.990
-(sighs)
-It's a Christian youth camp

21:34.125 --> 21:35.485
up near Silverthorne.

21:35.620 --> 21:37.086
What's this?

21:37.222 --> 21:38.820
They're accepting
applications for CITs

21:38.956 --> 21:40.259
for middle school winter camp.

21:40.394 --> 21:41.822
What's a CIT?

21:41.957 --> 21:43.829
Counselor in training.

21:44.936 --> 21:46.602
No... (stammers)

21:46.738 --> 21:48.932
I'm not going to be a counselor
for junior highers

21:49.068 --> 21:51.299
at some weird Jesus camp
you dreamed about.

21:51.434 --> 21:53.869
No, you're going to be
a counselor in training.

21:54.005 --> 21:55.709
-No, I'm not.
-Come on.

21:55.844 --> 21:57.608
Dad has been hounding you
to get a job,

21:57.743 --> 21:59.273
and this is a job that pays.

21:59.408 --> 22:01.346
-And we can find out what Mom...
-I said no.

22:01.482 --> 22:03.415
(footsteps approaching)

22:03.551 --> 22:05.315
What's going on in here?

22:05.451 --> 22:10.218
Uh, Gwen wants us to get jobs
at some Christian winter camp.

22:12.425 --> 22:14.662
Not Camp Alpine.

22:15.764 --> 22:17.759
-Hmm.
-(flipping through brochure)

22:17.895 --> 22:19.095
Your mother worked there.

22:22.038 --> 22:23.473
Wh-When?

22:24.476 --> 22:26.801
Uh, it was
long before I met her.

22:26.936 --> 22:29.806
It closed in '58.

22:29.941 --> 22:32.146
How'd you hear about this place?

22:32.281 --> 22:34.478
Uh, um, I-I had...

22:34.614 --> 22:36.178
Some kids at school.

22:36.313 --> 22:39.489
Said it was a good way
to, uh, make some money.

22:41.487 --> 22:43.526
Christian camp.

22:45.924 --> 22:48.356
You guys, you know I don't...

22:48.491 --> 22:50.693
much like any of that
religion stuff, you know?

22:50.829 --> 22:53.228
It-it's just a job, Dad.

22:54.565 --> 22:56.407
(groans)

22:58.868 --> 23:00.471
Mom worked there.

23:00.606 --> 23:02.479
I'm not crazy.

23:03.974 --> 23:06.516
I never said you were crazy.

23:08.886 --> 23:10.679
TERRENCE: Don't let me hear
you took that thing

23:10.815 --> 23:12.914
any faster than 55.

23:13.049 --> 23:14.425
ERNESTO:
Y-Yes, sir.

23:14.560 --> 23:16.326
I would like my daughter back
unscathed.

23:16.461 --> 23:18.660
-Do you understand?
-Yes, sir.

23:20.331 --> 23:21.898
Do you say anything else?

23:22.033 --> 23:23.197
Yes, sir.

23:23.333 --> 23:25.194
Uh, uh, I-I mean...

23:26.901 --> 23:29.137
I don't like the way
he looks at her.

23:29.272 --> 23:31.266
Yeah. Me, neither.

23:32.572 --> 23:34.269
Damn it. Wait.

23:35.542 --> 23:36.711
"Wait," what?

23:48.718 --> 23:49.785
Good.

23:49.921 --> 23:52.089
Go look after your sister.

23:53.794 --> 23:55.427
Do me a favor while I'm gone.

23:55.563 --> 23:57.265
Yeah, anything, Son.

23:57.401 --> 23:59.503
(sighs) Don't get drunk.

24:01.040 --> 24:02.739
Hey, come on.

24:02.875 --> 24:05.608
When are you gonna believe
I'm done with all of that?

24:05.743 --> 24:08.641
In two weeks,
I get my three-year chip.

24:08.776 --> 24:11.005
I'll have it when you get back.

24:11.140 --> 24:13.811
(sighs) See you in a few weeks.

24:13.946 --> 24:15.751
(chuckling):
Okay. Great.

24:15.886 --> 24:18.720
Finally get some peace and quiet
around this place.

24:19.789 --> 24:22.221
-(short chuckle)
-(door opens and closes)

24:22.356 --> 24:25.463
("Another Brick in the Wall,
Part 1" by Pink Floyd playing)

24:27.061 --> 24:32.426
♪ A snapshot
in the family album ♪

24:37.072 --> 24:42.546
♪ Daddy, what else
did you leave for me? ♪

24:49.119 --> 24:52.655
♪ Daddy, what'd you leave
behind for me? ♪

24:56.929 --> 25:02.324
♪ All in all, it was
just a brick in the wall ♪

25:06.631 --> 25:11.168
♪ All in all, it was
all just bricks in the wall. ♪

25:15.377 --> 25:17.581
♪ ♪

25:43.837 --> 25:45.900
I can't see the road.

25:46.035 --> 25:48.074
This isn't safe.

25:48.209 --> 25:50.746
We could drive off a cliff
and not even see it.

25:52.976 --> 25:54.585
Stop the car.

25:55.483 --> 25:56.515
(Finn sighs)

25:56.651 --> 25:57.983
What are you doing?

25:58.119 --> 25:59.453
I'm gonna run
in front of the car

25:59.588 --> 26:01.684
so I can see the road.

26:01.819 --> 26:03.422
Just follow me.

26:03.558 --> 26:05.853
(wind howling)

26:05.988 --> 26:08.599
♪ ♪

26:20.838 --> 26:22.107
Follow me!

26:28.878 --> 26:30.318
Mando!

26:30.454 --> 26:32.986
I found your stray CITs.

26:43.702 --> 26:45.563
MANDO:
Straight ahead about 20 yards.

26:45.699 --> 26:47.495
Park anywhere.

26:52.243 --> 26:53.407
Thank you.

26:53.543 --> 26:54.940
You must be the Blakes.

26:55.076 --> 26:56.404
FINN:
Yeah, how'd you know?

26:56.540 --> 26:58.641
MANDO: Oh, they closed I-6
at Silverthorne.

26:58.776 --> 27:01.745
You're the only ones
who didn't get the call in time.

27:01.880 --> 27:02.979
I'm Armando.

27:03.114 --> 27:04.953
Or just Mando, if you like.

27:05.088 --> 27:07.955
Come on. Come with me.
Let's get you inside.

27:09.726 --> 27:11.289
FINN:
What about all the kids?

27:11.424 --> 27:13.595
Aren't they supposed
to arrive tomorrow?

27:13.730 --> 27:15.799
MANDO:
Camp's canceled.

27:15.935 --> 27:19.328
They won't plow the roads
until the storm passes.

27:19.463 --> 27:21.601
GWEN:
How many people made it here?

27:21.736 --> 27:23.366
MANDO:
Just you three.

27:23.501 --> 27:26.167
Support staff has only
been here a week,

27:26.303 --> 27:28.077
but otherwise, you're it.

27:28.212 --> 27:31.407
I'm sorry to say it,
but for now you're stuck here.

27:34.285 --> 27:36.379
♪ ♪

27:43.253 --> 27:44.959
MUSTANG:
Come on, Gwen.

27:45.924 --> 27:47.962
You're with me.

27:49.031 --> 27:51.130
This is it.
Take any bunk you want.

27:51.266 --> 27:55.299
Heaters are on,
so just give 'em a few minutes.

27:55.434 --> 27:58.938
It will be toasty in no time,
all right?

27:59.074 --> 28:01.679
Have a good night, kids.
Sweet dreams.

28:01.814 --> 28:04.147
GWEN:
<i> I got to sleep in here alone?</i>

28:04.282 --> 28:05.406
Afraid so.

28:05.541 --> 28:06.581
State law requires
separate housing

28:06.716 --> 28:08.517
for male and female minors.

28:08.653 --> 28:10.083
I'd stay in here with you,

28:10.219 --> 28:12.954
but I'm not a registered
counselor, so no can do.

28:14.488 --> 28:18.025
But my cabin is just over there,
if you need anything.

28:19.890 --> 28:21.494
Night.

28:21.630 --> 28:23.833
(wind howling)

28:44.015 --> 28:46.251
(lighter clicking)

29:00.835 --> 29:02.938
(wind continues howling)

29:17.488 --> 29:18.947
(static crackling)

29:19.082 --> 29:21.825
♪ ♪

29:36.869 --> 29:38.974
♪ ♪

29:53.622 --> 29:55.749
♪ ♪

30:04.027 --> 30:06.094
(gasps)

30:06.230 --> 30:08.333
(wind continues howling)

30:14.270 --> 30:17.639
(static crackling)

30:20.110 --> 30:22.446
(phone ringing)

30:32.397 --> 30:34.590
(ringing stops)

30:36.929 --> 30:39.331
(scraping)

30:47.337 --> 30:50.012
(scraping continues)

30:50.976 --> 30:53.180
(phone ringing)

31:11.001 --> 31:13.200
I'm sorry, but I can't help you.

31:16.707 --> 31:18.374
(breathing heavily)

31:18.509 --> 31:21.010
(phone ringing)

31:24.308 --> 31:26.543
(prolonged ringing)

31:34.793 --> 31:36.894
(prolonged ringing continues)

31:40.322 --> 31:41.565
Who is this?

31:41.700 --> 31:43.967
(static droning over phone)

31:45.228 --> 31:47.366
♪ ♪

31:59.341 --> 32:02.216
(scraping)

32:25.444 --> 32:28.077
♪ ♪

32:29.205 --> 32:31.304
Hello?

32:31.439 --> 32:32.773
Is anyone there?

32:32.908 --> 32:35.018
THE GRABBER (over phone):
Hello, Finney.

32:37.918 --> 32:39.957
(grunting)

32:42.927 --> 32:45.693
-(phone ringing)
-(yelling)

32:45.829 --> 32:48.097
(breathing heavily)

32:52.596 --> 32:54.928
-(sizzling)
-(startled yelp)

32:57.740 --> 32:59.002
(phone ringing)

32:59.137 --> 33:00.142
(ringing stops)

33:12.553 --> 33:16.290
THE GRABBER:
Hell is not flames, Finney.

33:17.288 --> 33:18.451
It's ice.

33:18.587 --> 33:20.294
(breathing heavily)

33:23.492 --> 33:25.365
(Gwen whimpering)

33:30.769 --> 33:33.835
THE GRABBER:
Nothing burns like the cold.

33:37.340 --> 33:39.775
(gasping weakly)

33:42.983 --> 33:45.187
(screaming)

33:46.558 --> 33:48.553
(gasping weakly)

33:49.154 --> 33:50.925
(Gwen screaming)

33:51.060 --> 33:52.693
(Gwen screaming in distance)

33:52.828 --> 33:54.697
Gwen. Gwen!

33:54.832 --> 33:56.390
(screaming continues)

33:56.525 --> 33:58.295
Gwen, Gwen, Gwen!

33:58.430 --> 33:59.861
Hey, Gwen, Gwen, look at me!

33:59.996 --> 34:02.035
Hey, hey, look at me!
Wake up! Wake up!

34:02.170 --> 34:04.597
-(sobbing)
-Hey, hey.

34:04.733 --> 34:07.435
What's happening to me?

34:07.570 --> 34:09.340
Oh, God, I feel crazy.

34:09.475 --> 34:10.705
You were dreaming. You're okay.

34:10.841 --> 34:12.409
-You're okay.
-I feel crazy.

34:12.544 --> 34:14.045
You're okay. You're okay.

34:14.181 --> 34:16.581
(continues sobbing)

34:18.022 --> 34:20.722
You're okay. You're okay.

34:20.857 --> 34:22.455
You're okay.

34:25.323 --> 34:27.427
(wind howling)

34:54.251 --> 34:55.917
Gwen.

34:58.521 --> 35:00.493
I had a bad dream.

35:01.560 --> 35:04.299
Okay. Y-You... you all right?

35:08.763 --> 35:11.064
Here, uh... lie down.

35:19.608 --> 35:21.745
(wind howling)

35:32.927 --> 35:34.461
Jesus...

35:35.895 --> 35:38.896
please don't let me have
another dream tonight.

35:39.032 --> 35:40.830
Please.

35:41.870 --> 35:43.936
Hey.

35:44.071 --> 35:46.608
Y-You okay?

35:46.743 --> 35:48.270
Yeah.

35:48.405 --> 35:50.444
Did I wake you?

35:51.682 --> 35:53.381
No.

35:54.819 --> 35:57.652
Was that for real?

35:57.787 --> 35:59.682
What?

35:59.817 --> 36:03.820
You talk to Jesus
just like that?

36:05.256 --> 36:06.620
Yeah.

36:06.756 --> 36:08.997
You think it's weird?

36:09.132 --> 36:11.828
Uh, no. No, not-not at all.

36:12.961 --> 36:15.469
I th... I think it's hot.

36:16.936 --> 36:20.168
You think it's hot
that I talk to Jesus?

36:20.304 --> 36:23.210
Yeah. I mean, it might even
be hotter if you called him

36:23.345 --> 36:25.577
(Spanish pronunciation):
Jesús.

36:25.713 --> 36:28.548
You know, my mom is
Catholic as hell.

36:28.684 --> 36:31.914
She'd love me dating
somebody who prays.

36:33.517 --> 36:35.853
We're dating?

36:35.989 --> 36:39.555
Uh, um, I mean, I was...
I was just saying that...

36:39.691 --> 36:41.858
I'm a good Christian girl?

36:43.459 --> 36:44.731
Sure.

36:44.867 --> 36:46.533
Why not?

36:49.700 --> 36:51.901
My mom was Christian, too.

36:53.238 --> 36:56.671
Dad didn't want us brought up
in the church, but...

36:56.806 --> 36:59.040
I asked a lot of questions.

37:00.342 --> 37:04.045
And when he wasn't around,
she answered.

37:05.147 --> 37:07.950
Did she know
about your dream thing?

37:10.059 --> 37:12.152
I got it from her.

37:13.998 --> 37:16.057
It drove her crazy.

37:18.030 --> 37:20.765
I'm scared the same thing
will happen to me.

37:22.170 --> 37:24.205
It won't.

37:24.340 --> 37:26.573
You're too strong for that.

37:33.680 --> 37:35.747
You don't think I'm a freak?

37:36.946 --> 37:39.449
What's wrong with being a freak?

37:39.585 --> 37:41.852
I'm a freak like my mom.

37:43.060 --> 37:45.694
Were you close to her?

37:45.829 --> 37:47.931
Yeah.

37:48.066 --> 37:51.090
I think about her every day.

37:51.226 --> 37:53.765
I can still see her face
so clearly.

37:55.071 --> 37:57.131
She was beautiful.

37:59.067 --> 38:02.576
I think... you're beautiful.

38:10.919 --> 38:13.715
FINN: What about me?
Do you think I'm beautiful?

38:13.851 --> 38:15.786
Finn, you rotting shit stain.

38:15.921 --> 38:18.319
Have you been listening
this whole time?

38:18.455 --> 38:19.755
(sighs)

38:19.890 --> 38:21.957
Well, I'm still right here,

38:22.093 --> 38:24.796
so it's not like
I had any choice.

38:26.634 --> 38:28.371
ERNESTO:
I-I thought he was asleep.

38:29.404 --> 38:31.099
Told you Duran Duran is a date.

38:37.983 --> 38:40.207
(wind continues howling)

38:46.621 --> 38:49.986
Ernesto, I need to talk
to Gwen alone.

38:50.121 --> 38:53.862
If it's about last night,
he knows.

38:53.997 --> 38:55.098
Knows what?

38:55.233 --> 38:56.593
Why do you think he's here?

38:56.728 --> 38:58.631
He came to help us investigate.

38:58.766 --> 39:00.698
Wait, you told him
about your dreams?

39:00.834 --> 39:04.196
Hmm. Yeah, Finn,
I know about her dreams.

39:04.332 --> 39:06.574
And about the calls
that you get.

39:07.806 --> 39:09.674
-Gwen.
-We can trust him.

39:09.810 --> 39:13.611
Okay, but it wasn't
yours to tell.

39:13.746 --> 39:15.109
Okay, I haven't told anyone.

39:15.245 --> 39:16.776
Because you don't have
any friends.

39:16.912 --> 39:19.151
I... I have friends.

39:19.286 --> 39:20.653
Name one.

39:20.788 --> 39:22.317
One you've brought home
to hang out.

39:22.453 --> 39:24.622
One you've even mentioned
in a conversation at all.

39:24.757 --> 39:26.953
Gwen, it wasn't yours to tell.

39:27.089 --> 39:28.726
I have to tell somebody, Finn.

39:28.862 --> 39:30.695
You never want to hear
about my dreams.

39:30.831 --> 39:33.335
-That's not true.
-See this?

39:33.471 --> 39:36.032
This happened last night
in my dream.

39:37.208 --> 39:40.041
One of the kids grabbed me.

39:40.177 --> 39:42.776
In... in your dream?

39:42.911 --> 39:45.571
-Gwen, this is bad.
-MANDO: Morning, campers!

39:45.707 --> 39:50.053
Another glorious God-given day
here at Camp Alpine Lake.

39:50.188 --> 39:51.844
Breakfast in the mess hall.

39:51.980 --> 39:54.050
Come get some grub!

40:08.699 --> 40:12.739
(speaking Spanish)

40:15.880 --> 40:20.549
News reports say this is
the worst blizzard since '46.

40:21.845 --> 40:23.277
Denver is shut down.

40:23.413 --> 40:25.686
Best-case scenario is
two days, maybe three.

40:25.821 --> 40:27.916
-It could be longer.
-(footsteps approaching)

40:28.051 --> 40:29.625
You've met my niece Mustang.

40:29.761 --> 40:32.589
She works the stables
and in the kitchen with me.

40:32.724 --> 40:35.091
Mustang? Like the car?

40:36.198 --> 40:37.962
Like the horse.

40:40.967 --> 40:42.968
Uh, how many other people
are here?

40:43.103 --> 40:46.606
Just Kenneth and Barbara,
who run the offices.

40:46.741 --> 40:48.408
Rest of the support staff
got out

40:48.544 --> 40:51.411
before they closed the roads.

40:51.546 --> 40:54.877
So, how did everyone sleep?

40:55.012 --> 40:56.618
-ERNESTO: Fine.
-FINN: Fine.

40:57.917 --> 40:59.646
I noticed you slept
with the boys.

40:59.781 --> 41:02.349
I can lose my camp license
for that. Don't do it again.

41:04.758 --> 41:08.955
Now, for the $64,000 question:

41:09.090 --> 41:12.095
Why are you guys here?

41:13.829 --> 41:15.862
To be camp CITs.

41:15.998 --> 41:17.670
(chuckles) No, I...

41:17.806 --> 41:19.466
(clicks tongue)
I get that. (stammers)

41:19.602 --> 41:22.469
I mean, none of you
ever attended here as campers,

41:22.605 --> 41:25.847
and none of you listed churches
on your applications,

41:25.982 --> 41:29.343
so that means you didn't get
one of our flyers.

41:30.914 --> 41:33.853
So, why are you here?

41:40.154 --> 41:42.191
Huh? (speaks Spanish)

41:43.265 --> 41:45.326
(speaks Spanish)

41:46.367 --> 41:47.669
(chuckles)

41:49.635 --> 41:50.936
Our mom went here.

41:52.067 --> 41:54.608
Oh. Camper or counselor?

41:54.743 --> 41:56.879
Counselor.
Her name was Hope Adler.

41:57.014 --> 41:58.548
"Was"?

41:59.647 --> 42:01.347
She died seven years ago.

42:01.482 --> 42:03.520
Mm. I'm sorry.

42:04.849 --> 42:06.149
Do you remember her?

42:07.391 --> 42:09.222
A lot of kids come through here.

42:09.357 --> 42:10.918
(mutters)

42:11.054 --> 42:12.419
Do you know her camp name?

42:13.788 --> 42:16.326
Support staff and counselors,
they get camp names.

42:16.462 --> 42:20.295
It's easier for the campers
to remember who's who.

42:25.208 --> 42:27.038
Starlight.

42:28.710 --> 42:30.640
You're Starlight's kids?

42:30.776 --> 42:33.044
You do remember her.

42:34.151 --> 42:35.308
Very well.

42:35.443 --> 42:38.247
Sh-She was a true light,
that one.

42:42.251 --> 42:45.287
Um, I-I'm sorry you lost her.

42:47.695 --> 42:50.391
May I ask how she passed?

42:52.732 --> 42:54.835
She killed herself.

42:57.739 --> 43:00.874
(sighs) I-I... I'm so sorry.

43:06.150 --> 43:08.616
Look, I...

43:08.752 --> 43:11.544
I-I'm just glad
you guys found us.

43:12.757 --> 43:14.787
After you eat,
you should call your families

43:14.922 --> 43:17.120
and let 'em know you're okay.

43:17.255 --> 43:20.221
There's a phone
in the camp offices.

43:20.357 --> 43:22.797
Wait, what about
the outside pay phone?

43:22.932 --> 43:25.434
(scoffs)
That thing's deader than disco.

43:25.569 --> 43:27.527
Hasn't worked in over a decade.

43:31.276 --> 43:34.433
(door opens and closes)

43:34.569 --> 43:37.245
That dead pay phone rang
last night.

43:37.380 --> 43:39.311
Did you answer it?

43:39.446 --> 43:40.911
Yeah.

43:41.046 --> 43:42.742
I'm pretty sure it was him.

43:42.878 --> 43:44.185
Him?

43:44.320 --> 43:46.352
Like, "him" him?

43:46.487 --> 43:47.783
Oh, my God.

43:47.919 --> 43:49.751
What'd he say?

43:49.886 --> 43:52.453
-(phone ringing in distance)
-(stammering): What'd he want?

43:54.897 --> 43:56.657
-What?
-GWEN: It's ringing again?

43:56.793 --> 44:00.065
FINN: Go call Dad.
I'll meet you when I'm done.

44:00.965 --> 44:03.464
(ringing continues)

44:07.401 --> 44:08.937
(static droning over phone)

44:09.073 --> 44:10.805
You got something to say?

44:10.940 --> 44:13.144
Then say it.

44:13.280 --> 44:15.377
BOY (over phone, staticky):
It's cold here.

44:17.683 --> 44:19.381
Who is this?

44:21.117 --> 44:22.989
I don't remember.

44:23.955 --> 44:25.857
What happened to you?

44:25.992 --> 44:27.925
BOY 2:
We don't know.

44:28.060 --> 44:30.192
You don't remember anything?

44:30.327 --> 44:31.761
BOY 1:
There's three of us.

44:31.897 --> 44:34.193
Okay. Where are you?

44:34.329 --> 44:35.666
BOY 1:
It's cold here.

44:35.801 --> 44:37.630
It's cold where?

44:38.939 --> 44:40.677
BOY 3:
And it's dark here.

44:42.204 --> 44:43.809
Tell me where you are.

44:43.944 --> 44:45.748
BOY 3:
We don't know.

44:47.812 --> 44:49.748
My name is Finn.

44:49.883 --> 44:51.820
BOY 2:
Help us, Finn.

44:52.922 --> 44:55.256
You have to try
to remember something.

44:55.391 --> 44:57.791
How did you die?

44:57.926 --> 45:00.527
BOY 2:
We don't remember.

45:00.663 --> 45:02.560
We're scared, Finn.

45:02.696 --> 45:04.494
I understand.

45:04.630 --> 45:07.396
-Okay, what do you...
-We're not supposed to be here.

45:08.867 --> 45:10.199
What do you mean?

45:10.335 --> 45:12.167
BOY 2:
This isn't where we belong.

45:12.302 --> 45:14.744
We weren't supposed to be here.

45:17.043 --> 45:19.545
Something bad happened to you?

45:19.681 --> 45:22.548
Help us. Please help us.

45:22.683 --> 45:24.385
FINN:
Tell me.

45:24.521 --> 45:26.215
Tell me how I can help.

45:26.351 --> 45:27.823
BOY 1:
Find us, Finn. Please, Finn.

45:27.959 --> 45:29.523
-Help us! Please come find us!
-Come find us!

45:29.659 --> 45:31.390
You have to come find us!

45:31.525 --> 45:34.229
-We don't want to be here!
-(boys all shouting at once)

45:34.364 --> 45:36.392
(shouting stops)

45:39.501 --> 45:41.595
♪ ♪

45:49.946 --> 45:51.774
(over TV):
♪ Time to put aside... ♪

45:51.909 --> 45:54.713
TERRENCE (chuckles): Yeah,
we're snowed in here, as well.

45:54.849 --> 45:56.415
You guys just hold tight.

45:56.550 --> 45:58.755
I'm sure they'll have you
out of there in no time.

46:00.050 --> 46:01.758
Love you, kid.

46:03.260 --> 46:04.617
Bye.

46:04.752 --> 46:06.254
(over TV):
♪ Head for Busch Beer ♪

46:06.389 --> 46:09.965
♪ Head for the mountains. ♪

46:10.100 --> 46:12.528
REPORTER (over TV):
Welcome back to KMGH News.

46:12.663 --> 46:15.103
The blizzard brought
the entire area to a standstill

46:15.239 --> 46:17.797
as heavy winds and drifts
made all the roads impassable.

46:17.932 --> 46:19.838
-(rotary telephone dialing)
-So much so that police

46:19.973 --> 46:21.810
in several cities issued curfews

46:21.946 --> 46:24.139
against the vehicles
being on the road.

46:24.274 --> 46:26.077
And the restrictions still stand

46:26.213 --> 46:28.283
to those who violate
the order...

46:28.418 --> 46:30.049
Yeah, Jake, hey.

46:30.185 --> 46:33.088
Listen, I need to call in
that favor.

46:33.223 --> 46:36.991
Has the company fleet
finished plowing the property?

46:38.090 --> 46:41.094
(Ernesto speaking Spanish)

46:49.431 --> 46:52.107
GWEN:
Excuse me.

46:52.243 --> 46:54.767
Do you have any literature
on the history of Alpine Lake?

46:57.009 --> 47:00.212
Uh, we have a brochure.

47:01.146 --> 47:03.844
Damn. Nothing more in-depth?

47:03.980 --> 47:08.188
No, there is no published
history of Camp Alpine Lake.

47:08.323 --> 47:10.921
We are a youth camp,
not a historical society.

47:11.057 --> 47:13.627
Barbara, these are guests.

47:13.763 --> 47:15.357
BARBARA:
No, Kenneth,

47:15.493 --> 47:17.296
this is the young lady
who decided

47:17.431 --> 47:21.398
to sneak into the boys' cabin
last night.

47:21.533 --> 47:24.136
So, what exactly
can we help you with, sweetie?

47:24.272 --> 47:27.172
Look, we just want to know
about some kids

47:27.308 --> 47:31.871
that may have been
killed here in the past.

47:32.006 --> 47:33.711
You don't need to hear
anything about that.

47:33.847 --> 47:35.449
We don't?

47:35.585 --> 47:37.848
You don't.

47:37.984 --> 47:40.118
Philippians 4:8 tells us

47:40.253 --> 47:42.188
to think on things
that are lovely.

47:43.325 --> 47:45.224
Philippians 4:8 also says
to think on things

47:45.359 --> 47:48.161
that are true, just and honest,
right, Barb?

47:49.366 --> 47:50.890
Barbara.

47:51.025 --> 47:52.759
(stammering):
We don't know the specifics.

47:52.894 --> 47:55.771
This is not some haunted tour
or ghost camp.

47:55.906 --> 47:57.600
This is
a Christian organization.

47:57.736 --> 47:59.766
We don't discuss
those kinds of things here.

47:59.901 --> 48:02.670
But some fucked-up shit
did happen here, right?

48:04.280 --> 48:07.346
Have you always had
such a filthy, vulgar mouth?

48:07.481 --> 48:10.250
Have you always been
such a sanctimonious twat?

48:10.385 --> 48:14.187
Hey, hey, I-I think
you two should leave now.

48:16.054 --> 48:17.685
Let's go.

48:19.058 --> 48:20.787
I'll pray for you.

48:25.162 --> 48:27.629
(owl hooting)

48:34.668 --> 48:36.770
(phone ringing in distance)

48:38.747 --> 48:41.115
(static crackling)

48:42.014 --> 48:43.777
(inhales sharply)

48:44.718 --> 48:46.613
Hello?

48:46.749 --> 48:48.620
BOY 1 (over phone):
Who is this?

48:48.755 --> 48:50.249
Hope.

48:50.384 --> 48:52.427
Uh, Hope Adler.

48:52.562 --> 48:54.056
Who is this?

48:54.191 --> 48:56.123
I can't see you.

48:56.259 --> 48:57.498
Where are you?

48:57.633 --> 48:59.496
Alpine Lake.

49:01.369 --> 49:04.231
It's a youth camp
in the mountains.

49:04.366 --> 49:06.134
It's so dark.

49:06.270 --> 49:08.400
How did you find me?

49:08.536 --> 49:11.039
I had these dreams.

49:11.175 --> 49:13.213
Seven numbers.

49:14.381 --> 49:16.543
No area code,
so this call is local.

49:16.678 --> 49:18.955
You're here in Colorado, right?

49:19.888 --> 49:22.024
Where were the numbers?

49:23.057 --> 49:25.120
The numbers were carved in ice.

49:25.255 --> 49:26.692
The ice of a lake?

49:26.827 --> 49:29.790
Yes. Yes!

49:29.926 --> 49:32.162
BOY 1: It's so hard
to remember things here.

49:32.297 --> 49:33.932
It's so cold and dark.

49:34.068 --> 49:36.372
HOPE:
Who is this?

49:36.507 --> 49:38.302
Who are you?

49:38.437 --> 49:40.333
BOY 1:
We don't remember.

49:40.469 --> 49:42.143
HOPE:
Hello?

49:43.241 --> 49:44.944
Hello? Can you hear me?

49:45.079 --> 49:46.410
(static droning over phone)

49:46.545 --> 49:47.940
-(high-pitched tone over phone)
-(yelps)

49:48.075 --> 49:50.085
BOY 1:
We're not supposed to be here.

49:53.623 --> 49:56.454
♪ ♪

50:10.068 --> 50:12.173
♪ ♪

50:32.662 --> 50:34.756
♪ ♪

50:42.299 --> 50:45.140
(muffled banging)

50:47.711 --> 50:50.211
(loud banging)

50:55.010 --> 50:57.845
-(wind howling)
-(door continues banging)

51:05.662 --> 51:07.855
(phone ringing)

51:11.693 --> 51:13.828
(ringing continues in distance)

51:16.034 --> 51:16.998
Ernesto!

51:17.134 --> 51:18.536
Wake up!

51:19.401 --> 51:21.539
(audio muffled)

51:22.470 --> 51:24.674
♪ ♪

51:46.560 --> 51:49.028
(phone ringing)

51:49.164 --> 51:51.272
ERNESTO: You don't
have to answer it, man.

51:52.272 --> 51:53.901
FINN:
Yes, I do.

51:56.676 --> 52:00.479
You have one job:
look after my sister.

52:01.619 --> 52:03.279
I promise.

52:03.415 --> 52:05.620
(phone continues ringing)

52:05.755 --> 52:07.849
♪ ♪

52:29.911 --> 52:32.473
♪ ♪

52:32.609 --> 52:34.110
(phone continues ringing)

52:34.245 --> 52:36.448
(ringing stops)

52:36.583 --> 52:38.649
THE GRABBER (over phone):
Hello, Finney.

52:41.616 --> 52:43.984
What do you want?

52:44.119 --> 52:49.324
It took me a long time,
but now I remember.

52:49.459 --> 52:51.523
You're dead.

52:51.658 --> 52:53.697
Oh, Finney.

52:54.762 --> 52:57.972
You of all people know

52:58.107 --> 53:01.034
that "dead" is just a word.

53:05.477 --> 53:07.480
Tell me why you're here.

53:09.009 --> 53:11.385
Why do you think I'm here?

53:12.453 --> 53:14.553
'Cause you knew we'd be trapped.

53:16.156 --> 53:18.055
ERNESTO:
Gwen?

53:18.190 --> 53:21.955
Gwen! Gwen!

53:22.091 --> 53:24.728
-(wind howling)
-(door creaks, bangs shut)

53:37.814 --> 53:40.007
♪ ♪

53:59.561 --> 54:01.765
♪ ♪

54:19.218 --> 54:21.422
♪ ♪

54:24.695 --> 54:29.793
THE GRABBER: Did you think
that our story was over, Finney?

54:31.161 --> 54:35.795
Did you really believe
you could do what you did to me

54:35.930 --> 54:37.433
and that would be the end of it?

54:37.569 --> 54:39.336
I'm not afraid of you.

54:39.471 --> 54:41.006
And why should you be?

54:41.142 --> 54:42.673
You killed me.

54:42.808 --> 54:45.111
-You won.
-(Finn breathing heavily)

54:45.246 --> 54:46.478
Tell me what you want.

54:46.613 --> 54:50.311
What I have always
wanted with you.

54:50.446 --> 54:51.645
What?

54:51.780 --> 54:53.652
You want to scare me?

54:56.224 --> 54:59.324
You know as well as I do

54:59.460 --> 55:03.431
that fear is just the warm-up.

55:05.736 --> 55:07.193
Gwen!

55:08.137 --> 55:09.602
-Gwen!
-Hey!

55:09.737 --> 55:12.308
-(Ernesto gasps)
-Hey! What are you doing?

55:13.441 --> 55:15.010
It's 3:00 in the morning.

55:15.146 --> 55:16.539
G-Gwen isn't in her dorm.

55:16.675 --> 55:18.307
I don't know where she is.

55:18.442 --> 55:20.646
♪ ♪

55:41.268 --> 55:43.471
(flames rumbling)

55:45.338 --> 55:46.732
(loud clattering)

55:46.868 --> 55:49.070
(clattering in distance)

55:54.815 --> 55:57.353
THE GRABBER:
Have you guessed what it is yet?

55:58.518 --> 56:03.656
What it is that I want from you?

56:05.620 --> 56:09.695
THE GRABBER:<i> "Want" isn't even</i>
<i> the right word.</i>

56:09.830 --> 56:14.161
<i> It's more</i>
<i> of an insatiable need.</i>

56:15.799 --> 56:18.663
<i> So, have you got it yet?</i>

56:18.799 --> 56:20.267
<i> No?</i>

56:20.402 --> 56:23.335
<i> Fine.</i>
<i> I'll just tell you, Finney.</i>

56:24.676 --> 56:29.176
<i> What I want is this.</i>

56:31.714 --> 56:36.853
I want to hurt you

56:36.988 --> 56:40.757
in ways that
you can't even imagine.

56:40.893 --> 56:45.793
You will pay
for what you did to me.

56:45.928 --> 56:50.296
You made me kill my brother,

56:50.431 --> 56:55.834
the person on earth
that I loved the most!

56:55.970 --> 56:58.579
And then you killed me!

57:00.376 --> 57:05.113
<i> So now I am</i>
<i> going to destroy you, Finney...</i>

57:06.855 --> 57:10.954
<i> ...by destroying</i>
<i> the thing you love most.</i>

57:12.723 --> 57:17.462
<i> Vengeance is mine.</i>

57:17.597 --> 57:19.798
(The Grabber breathing heavily)

57:21.205 --> 57:23.300
(The Grabber chuckling)

57:23.435 --> 57:25.903
(yelping)

57:27.109 --> 57:29.445
(screams, gasps)

57:31.544 --> 57:34.443
(The Grabber straining)

57:34.578 --> 57:37.281
(both straining)

57:37.416 --> 57:38.980
(choking)

57:39.115 --> 57:40.746
-(growls)
-(Gwen gasping, choking)

57:40.881 --> 57:42.458
(door opens)

57:44.325 --> 57:46.088
(choking, gasping)

57:50.726 --> 57:52.464
(all screaming)

57:52.599 --> 57:54.364
(Gwen screaming over phone)

57:54.499 --> 57:57.264
Gwen! Gwen!

57:59.735 --> 58:02.104
(choking)

58:03.413 --> 58:05.481
-(screams)
-ERNESTO: Gwen!

58:07.150 --> 58:08.950
(Barbara gasping)

58:09.085 --> 58:11.718
(screaming)

58:21.692 --> 58:23.391
(Ernesto grunting)

58:23.527 --> 58:24.962
Help me!

58:25.859 --> 58:26.834
Help me!

58:26.970 --> 58:28.328
(grunts)

58:29.996 --> 58:32.138
(whimpering)

58:32.273 --> 58:34.774
(grunting)

58:36.610 --> 58:38.844
(Gwen continues screaming)

58:40.479 --> 58:42.342
(both grunting)

58:48.982 --> 58:51.824
♪ ♪

59:04.373 --> 59:06.131
Hey. Hey. Hey, Gwen.

59:06.267 --> 59:08.368
Gwen, wake up. Gwen, wake up.

59:09.513 --> 59:11.578
(muffled):
Gwen, are you awake?

59:11.713 --> 59:13.505
(louder):
Gwen, are you awake?

59:16.077 --> 59:17.685
(softly):
Hey.

59:21.083 --> 59:22.591
(clearly):
You awake?

59:26.187 --> 59:28.927
You got the devil in you, child.

59:29.958 --> 59:32.161
(footsteps pacing)

59:42.705 --> 59:43.744
(sighs)

59:48.179 --> 59:52.114
I've been on this earth
a lot of years.

59:52.249 --> 59:55.284
Seen a lot of things
I can't explain.

59:55.419 --> 59:57.215
But I've never heard of anyone
who got dreams

59:57.350 --> 59:59.494
like the ones you describe.

59:59.629 --> 01:00:01.019
Where do you think
they come from?

01:00:01.154 --> 01:00:02.562
She's possessed.

01:00:02.697 --> 01:00:04.799
My God, Mando, isn't it obvious?

01:00:04.934 --> 01:00:07.762
I'm not possessed,
you judgmental cunt wagon.

01:00:07.897 --> 01:00:09.569
(Mustang laughing)

01:00:09.704 --> 01:00:11.064
You think this is funny,
Mustang?

01:00:11.199 --> 01:00:13.404
You getting your horns clipped?

01:00:13.539 --> 01:00:14.907
Yeah, I do.

01:00:15.042 --> 01:00:16.103
Why don't you mind
your own business?

01:00:16.238 --> 01:00:17.912
Why don't you stop acting like

01:00:18.048 --> 01:00:19.144
this is the first creepy shit
you've seen up here?

01:00:19.280 --> 01:00:20.314
Stop it.

01:00:20.449 --> 01:00:21.978
Every single one of us

01:00:22.114 --> 01:00:24.585
has seen or heard things
around here.

01:00:24.721 --> 01:00:26.518
-You especially, Barb.
-Barbara.

01:00:26.653 --> 01:00:28.019
Shut up, both of you.

01:00:29.083 --> 01:00:32.627
Gwen, your dreams,

01:00:32.762 --> 01:00:35.389
are you saying
they tell you the future?

01:00:36.763 --> 01:00:38.560
GWEN:
Sometimes.

01:00:38.695 --> 01:00:41.829
Other times, it's the dead
showing me things from the past.

01:00:41.965 --> 01:00:43.228
What kind of things?

01:00:43.364 --> 01:00:45.839
Like the smallest missing boy.

01:00:47.143 --> 01:00:48.943
Felix?

01:00:49.079 --> 01:00:52.208
He was running for his life,
wearing a yellow down parka.

01:00:52.344 --> 01:00:55.478
A-And the tallest kid,
he wore a white parka.

01:00:55.613 --> 01:00:57.215
Spike.

01:00:57.350 --> 01:01:02.847
And scratched letters
into the ice above him: "WBH."

01:01:02.983 --> 01:01:05.921
I think his head was cut in half
on the tree stump in the woods.

01:01:06.056 --> 01:01:07.496
BARBARA:
Lord in heaven.

01:01:07.631 --> 01:01:09.824
The third boy wore
a denim jacket.

01:01:09.960 --> 01:01:12.161
He was all burnt up,

01:01:12.297 --> 01:01:14.593
like he'd been cooked
inside an oven.

01:01:16.103 --> 01:01:18.062
-How'd you know that?
-KENNETH: Mando.

01:01:18.198 --> 01:01:19.740
No. (stammers)

01:01:19.876 --> 01:01:23.808
Gwen, ignore everyone else
in the room.

01:01:23.943 --> 01:01:26.376
It's just you and me right now.

01:01:26.512 --> 01:01:30.378
The boy who was burnt up,
how did you hear about that?

01:01:31.452 --> 01:01:33.046
I just told you.

01:01:33.182 --> 01:01:34.954
He came to me in my dream.

01:01:35.953 --> 01:01:37.217
He wants me to find him.

01:01:37.352 --> 01:01:38.859
-They all do.
-(groans)

01:01:38.994 --> 01:01:40.551
They can't rest
until they're found.

01:01:40.687 --> 01:01:43.230
-Whoa. You okay there, Mando?
-Mando?

01:01:43.365 --> 01:01:45.096
(sighs heavily)

01:01:46.333 --> 01:01:50.701
Burnt pieces of
Calvin O'Keefe's denim jacket

01:01:50.836 --> 01:01:52.538
were found by police.

01:01:52.674 --> 01:01:54.842
Only they had that detail.

01:01:54.977 --> 01:01:58.044
The police,
the former camp owner and me.

01:01:58.179 --> 01:02:00.413
BARBARA: What about
what we saw in the kitchen?

01:02:00.548 --> 01:02:03.011
That was no dream.

01:02:03.147 --> 01:02:04.717
Have you heard of The Grabber?

01:02:04.852 --> 01:02:06.820
MANDO:
Yeah. Who hasn't?

01:02:06.956 --> 01:02:09.149
He killed a bunch of kids,
and then...

01:02:09.284 --> 01:02:11.517
got killed when one escaped.

01:02:11.653 --> 01:02:14.686
Yeah, h-his name was
Finney something.

01:02:19.061 --> 01:02:20.802
Finney Blake.

01:02:22.272 --> 01:02:23.464
Finn Blake?

01:02:24.835 --> 01:02:27.402
Holy shit.

01:02:28.909 --> 01:02:32.277
Gwen, when did all this start?

01:02:32.413 --> 01:02:36.110
Weeks ago, when my mom called me
from this camp in a dream.

01:02:36.245 --> 01:02:37.886
She wanted me to come here.

01:02:38.021 --> 01:02:40.879
Wh-What does this have to do
with The Grabber?

01:02:41.014 --> 01:02:43.015
It wasn't the devil
attacking me in the kitchen.

01:02:43.150 --> 01:02:44.449
It was him.

01:02:44.584 --> 01:02:46.753
I could see him. He's here.

01:02:46.889 --> 01:02:50.622
This is from the last year
of camp before we closed down.

01:02:50.757 --> 01:02:53.593
I-I was just the camp cook
back then.

01:02:53.728 --> 01:02:57.300
There's me,
and there's your mom.

01:02:58.601 --> 01:03:02.741
After Harlan, the owner,
closed this place,

01:03:02.877 --> 01:03:05.142
I kept coming up here anyway,

01:03:05.277 --> 01:03:08.542
hiking the area,
looking for those kids.

01:03:10.218 --> 01:03:12.282
Then, when Harlan passed,
I bought this place

01:03:12.417 --> 01:03:15.549
in an estate sale for a song
and reopened it.

01:03:15.685 --> 01:03:17.589
I promised their parents
I wouldn't stop looking

01:03:17.725 --> 01:03:19.122
until I found them.

01:03:19.257 --> 01:03:22.797
So, every day,
weather permitting,

01:03:22.933 --> 01:03:26.358
I'm still out
walking the trails,

01:03:26.493 --> 01:03:28.367
digging up every mound of dirt.

01:03:28.503 --> 01:03:31.262
Not a single morning goes by
that I don't pray for help

01:03:31.398 --> 01:03:33.666
to find those boys.

01:03:33.801 --> 01:03:36.339
I didn't know it was you
he'd send.

01:03:37.809 --> 01:03:42.015
But now that you're here,
I'm not gonna pass up a chance

01:03:42.151 --> 01:03:44.150
to put those kids to rest
once and for all,

01:03:44.285 --> 01:03:48.153
for-for-for them,
for their families and for me.

01:03:49.755 --> 01:03:51.020
No fucking way.

01:03:51.155 --> 01:03:52.784
What is it with this family?

01:03:53.797 --> 01:03:56.293
It's him. It's The Grabber.

01:03:56.428 --> 01:03:57.728
-MANDO: Are you sure?
-FINN: I know him,

01:03:57.864 --> 01:03:59.565
and I know his face.

01:03:59.700 --> 01:04:01.962
That's Bill.

01:04:02.097 --> 01:04:03.669
Wild Bill.

01:04:03.804 --> 01:04:04.972
He worked maintenance.

01:04:06.338 --> 01:04:08.305
(stammering):
We called him Wild Bill

01:04:08.440 --> 01:04:12.111
because he wore this
brown leather tool belt

01:04:12.246 --> 01:04:13.806
loose around his waist
like a gunslinger,

01:04:13.941 --> 01:04:17.314
and he got long, wavy hair
like Wild Bill Hickok.

01:04:19.588 --> 01:04:21.981
Wild Bill Hickok.

01:04:22.116 --> 01:04:23.617
"WBH."

01:04:24.485 --> 01:04:26.088
This is where he started.

01:04:26.223 --> 01:04:28.026
These boys were his first kills.

01:04:28.162 --> 01:04:29.856
And Wild Bill became
The Grabber.

01:04:29.992 --> 01:04:33.568
Mando, when did weird things
start happening around here?

01:04:33.704 --> 01:04:35.401
Mm, not until a few years ago.

01:04:35.536 --> 01:04:37.328
1978?

01:04:37.464 --> 01:04:39.069
Sounds about right.

01:04:39.204 --> 01:04:41.042
That's the year I killed him.

01:04:41.177 --> 01:04:43.138
And his spirit was set free
to come back here.

01:04:43.273 --> 01:04:45.474
Okay, but why would he do that?

01:04:46.877 --> 01:04:49.510
Maybe his spirit draws power
from the fear of his victims

01:04:49.646 --> 01:04:52.982
because their spirits
are not at rest.

01:04:53.118 --> 01:04:54.648
How do we find these boys?

01:04:56.018 --> 01:04:59.852
Their bodies are underwater,
in a frozen lake, I think.

01:04:59.987 --> 01:05:01.627
But didn't the police search
the local lakes?

01:05:01.763 --> 01:05:03.428
No. Why would they?

01:05:03.564 --> 01:05:05.065
The lakes were frozen over
when the boys went missing.

01:05:06.895 --> 01:05:09.934
Lake Maru is where
we take campers ice fishing,

01:05:10.069 --> 01:05:12.032
so we store our equipment there.

01:05:12.167 --> 01:05:13.668
(stammering)

01:05:13.804 --> 01:05:16.104
Wild Bill used it
for the kids' hockey games.

01:05:16.239 --> 01:05:17.937
He was a good skater.

01:05:18.073 --> 01:05:20.109
That's the only lake
where he would have the tools

01:05:20.244 --> 01:05:23.076
to make a hole in the ice and...

01:05:23.211 --> 01:05:24.612
dump the bodies.

01:05:24.747 --> 01:05:29.151
Okay, so i-if we find Felix,
Cal and Spike,

01:05:29.286 --> 01:05:32.752
allow them to rest, as you say,

01:05:32.887 --> 01:05:35.656
that would get rid
of The Grabber's power?

01:05:37.226 --> 01:05:39.396
I think so. Yeah.

01:05:41.229 --> 01:05:42.797
Okay, then.

01:05:42.933 --> 01:05:47.701
At dawn, we head to Lake Maru
and look for those boys.

01:06:02.058 --> 01:06:04.854
(staticky, warbling tone
over radio)

01:06:04.989 --> 01:06:06.995
(tone stops)

01:06:20.401 --> 01:06:23.511
(sighs, chuckles)

01:06:23.647 --> 01:06:25.937
Very funny, Mustang.

01:06:32.187 --> 01:06:35.551
(radio clicks on,
static crackling)

01:06:38.823 --> 01:06:42.961
THE GRABBER (over radio):
Look what you made me do.

01:06:43.096 --> 01:06:46.434
You made me kill my brother.

01:06:46.569 --> 01:06:48.531
♪ ♪

01:06:52.503 --> 01:06:54.835
I know you're out there, Bill.

01:06:55.805 --> 01:06:58.376
You can't have those boys
forever.

01:06:59.940 --> 01:07:04.316
THE GRABBER:
My name's not Bill.

01:07:05.513 --> 01:07:08.980
Wild Bill, Grabber.

01:07:09.989 --> 01:07:12.324
Evil is evil.

01:07:19.528 --> 01:07:22.466
(rummaging through drawers)

01:07:31.444 --> 01:07:34.742
(Mando taking
slow, deep breaths)

01:07:38.214 --> 01:07:40.187
(loud thud)

01:07:44.522 --> 01:07:47.594
THE GRABBER (over radio):
I want

01:07:47.729 --> 01:07:52.067
to hurt you.

01:07:57.701 --> 01:08:00.202
We are gonna get
those boys back, Bill.

01:08:00.338 --> 01:08:03.302
My name's not Bill!

01:08:03.437 --> 01:08:04.475
(loud thud)

01:08:06.881 --> 01:08:08.107
(radio clicks off)

01:08:08.243 --> 01:08:10.481
(sighs)

01:08:31.273 --> 01:08:33.773
The devil's lettuce
is not allowed

01:08:33.909 --> 01:08:36.441
in Camp Alpine property.

01:08:38.882 --> 01:08:40.845
FINN:
So fire me.

01:08:40.980 --> 01:08:42.579
(Mando chuckles)

01:08:45.612 --> 01:08:47.320
(Mando sighs)

01:08:49.152 --> 01:08:51.016
You've really been through it,
haven't you, kid?

01:08:58.801 --> 01:09:02.830
There's... there's a certain
look in a young man's eye.

01:09:04.005 --> 01:09:06.904
Kind of, um, quiet fury,

01:09:07.039 --> 01:09:08.606
kind of...

01:09:08.742 --> 01:09:12.477
deep rage when he's seen
too much or done too much.

01:09:18.614 --> 01:09:20.353
Get in many fights, Finn?

01:09:23.791 --> 01:09:24.924
So?

01:09:25.060 --> 01:09:27.591
So, here's what I know.

01:09:28.726 --> 01:09:32.530
Behind that kind of anger
is fear.

01:09:34.565 --> 01:09:35.928
I'm not afraid of anything.

01:09:36.064 --> 01:09:37.530
I know one thing
you're afraid of.

01:09:37.666 --> 01:09:40.032
Yeah? What's that?

01:09:40.167 --> 01:09:42.507
That you can't protect
your sister.

01:09:47.115 --> 01:09:49.574
When I was on the streets,

01:09:49.710 --> 01:09:51.647
I chose the wrong path.

01:09:51.783 --> 01:09:55.322
Instead of facing my fears,
I chose anger.

01:09:55.457 --> 01:09:57.258
You're doing the same.
I can see it.

01:09:59.495 --> 01:10:04.232
Finn, son... (stammers)
this is what I do for a living.

01:10:04.367 --> 01:10:07.995
I meet half a dozen kids
like you every year.

01:10:08.130 --> 01:10:11.866
Kids who are told
this is who they have to be.

01:10:13.702 --> 01:10:16.838
You are stronger than you think.

01:10:18.381 --> 01:10:20.845
You were strong enough
to kill The Grabber,

01:10:20.980 --> 01:10:24.311
and you are strong enough to
let what happened with him go.

01:10:24.446 --> 01:10:26.650
♪ ♪

01:10:28.949 --> 01:10:31.017
I don't know how to do that.

01:10:32.059 --> 01:10:33.893
You got to...

01:10:34.029 --> 01:10:37.091
face your feelings.

01:10:37.226 --> 01:10:39.895
You can't just hold them in
and numb it all out.

01:10:40.030 --> 01:10:42.567
You got to face it,
and then you can let it go.

01:10:44.868 --> 01:10:48.034
He wants to kill Gwen,
to hurt me.

01:10:48.169 --> 01:10:50.938
Oh, we're not gonna
let that happen.

01:11:01.223 --> 01:11:03.422
I'm taking this with me. (sighs)

01:11:03.558 --> 01:11:05.318
-Come on, man. I need that.
-(groans)

01:11:05.453 --> 01:11:07.625
I'm doing you a favor.
This ain't even good shit.

01:11:08.860 --> 01:11:12.559
We head to the lake
in an hour, at sunup.

01:11:12.694 --> 01:11:14.929
-Be ready.
-(sighs)

01:11:17.906 --> 01:11:20.099
♪ ♪

01:11:36.287 --> 01:11:38.491
♪ ♪

01:11:56.846 --> 01:11:59.039
♪ ♪

01:12:15.929 --> 01:12:19.764
Me and Ernesto are gonna
take shifts watching you, so...

01:12:19.899 --> 01:12:22.601
if you have another nightmare,
we'll wake you.

01:12:24.238 --> 01:12:26.099
What if you can't?

01:12:28.108 --> 01:12:30.005
Then fight back.

01:12:30.975 --> 01:12:32.809
I mean, it's your dream,
isn't it?

01:12:34.447 --> 01:12:36.945
He makes it more than that.

01:12:41.788 --> 01:12:45.251
What about those books
you read about dreaming?

01:12:45.387 --> 01:12:47.659
You know, there's got to be
something you can try.

01:12:48.822 --> 01:12:50.926
He's too strong.

01:12:51.726 --> 01:12:53.764
(sighs softly)

01:12:56.029 --> 01:12:58.197
I thought that once, too.

01:13:06.742 --> 01:13:08.205
She's out. (sighs)

01:13:08.341 --> 01:13:09.912
ERNESTO:
Can I ask you a question?

01:13:15.154 --> 01:13:17.722
Did you really talk to my
brother down in that basement?

01:13:19.895 --> 01:13:22.089
(sighs)

01:13:31.907 --> 01:13:33.434
Yeah.

01:13:33.569 --> 01:13:34.833
Yeah, I did.

01:13:34.968 --> 01:13:37.007
Wh-What'd he say?

01:13:37.143 --> 01:13:40.746
He said that your dad didn't
come back from Vietnam

01:13:40.882 --> 01:13:42.714
because he couldn't leave
his buddies behind.

01:13:44.345 --> 01:13:46.820
And that he wasn't gonna
leave me behind.

01:13:46.955 --> 01:13:48.555
Yeah?

01:13:49.691 --> 01:13:52.383
Yeah, that...
that was Robin all right.

01:13:55.859 --> 01:13:58.389
Do you think he's still here?

01:14:00.364 --> 01:14:04.764
I-I don't really know
what's on the other side,

01:14:04.900 --> 01:14:07.338
but there's something.

01:14:07.474 --> 01:14:09.301
And I hope it's good.

01:14:10.972 --> 01:14:12.771
And I hope he's there.

01:14:12.906 --> 01:14:15.439
But if he isn't,

01:14:15.574 --> 01:14:18.112
it's not me
he's here looking after.

01:14:21.718 --> 01:14:23.986
Wake me in four hours.

01:14:34.928 --> 01:14:35.936
(static crackling)

01:14:36.071 --> 01:14:38.231
♪ ♪

01:14:55.255 --> 01:14:57.624
♪ ♪

01:15:15.839 --> 01:15:18.704
(The Grabber groans, laughs)

01:15:18.839 --> 01:15:21.472
(cackling)

01:15:23.447 --> 01:15:24.381
(gasps)

01:15:24.517 --> 01:15:26.316
(breathing heavily)

01:15:26.451 --> 01:15:28.281
Wild Bill.

01:15:54.646 --> 01:15:56.416
Nope, nope, no, no.

01:15:56.551 --> 01:15:58.916
Y-You're staying in bed tonight.

01:16:00.521 --> 01:16:02.722
(static crackling softly)

01:16:09.164 --> 01:16:11.357
♪ ♪

01:16:31.186 --> 01:16:33.379
♪ ♪

01:16:50.271 --> 01:16:52.464
♪ ♪

01:17:13.085 --> 01:17:15.289
♪ ♪

01:17:38.319 --> 01:17:40.512
♪ ♪

01:17:56.799 --> 01:17:59.201
♪ ♪

01:18:13.520 --> 01:18:15.415
(voice muted)

01:18:34.804 --> 01:18:37.008
♪ ♪

01:18:54.523 --> 01:18:56.588
THE GRABBER:
You look like your mother.

01:19:00.161 --> 01:19:01.967
Why is she in here?

01:19:03.696 --> 01:19:06.266
THE GRABBER:
A kindness, really.

01:19:06.401 --> 01:19:09.810
To you, I mean.
A kindness to you.

01:19:11.170 --> 01:19:12.472
A kindness?

01:19:14.080 --> 01:19:16.212
THE GRABBER:
It's what I can manage.

01:19:19.217 --> 01:19:22.288
My mom dreamed about
Billy Showalter,

01:19:22.424 --> 01:19:24.153
the paperboy.

01:19:24.289 --> 01:19:26.585
He was the first kid taken
in our area.

01:19:28.228 --> 01:19:30.589
She figured out you took him,
didn't she?

01:19:33.000 --> 01:19:35.231
THE GRABBER:
Isn't that obvious?

01:19:37.197 --> 01:19:39.638
The kindness here

01:19:39.773 --> 01:19:42.608
is me showing you the truth

01:19:42.744 --> 01:19:45.608
before I do what I have to do.

01:19:45.743 --> 01:19:47.947
♪ ♪

01:19:59.020 --> 01:20:00.360
(gasping)

01:20:00.495 --> 01:20:02.989
Abandon all hope,

01:20:03.124 --> 01:20:06.031
ye who enter here.

01:20:07.966 --> 01:20:10.629
(Gwen gasping, whimpering)

01:20:17.914 --> 01:20:20.947
(voice shaking):
She didn't kill herself.

01:20:24.144 --> 01:20:26.513
You killed her!

01:20:30.190 --> 01:20:32.424
TERRENCE (whimpering):
No. No, no, no, no.

01:20:32.559 --> 01:20:34.017
No, no, no.

01:20:34.153 --> 01:20:35.286
No, no.

01:20:35.421 --> 01:20:36.762
(sobbing):
No!

01:20:36.897 --> 01:20:39.929
What did you do?
What did you do?

01:20:40.065 --> 01:20:42.432
What have I done? What have...

01:20:42.568 --> 01:20:44.663
No, no!

01:20:44.798 --> 01:20:47.336
THE GRABBER:
This is different than a dream.

01:20:48.204 --> 01:20:50.768
I conjured this from my hate

01:20:50.904 --> 01:20:54.275
and from whatever memories
hell let me keep.

01:20:54.410 --> 01:20:59.711
Hell is different
than you think.

01:20:59.846 --> 01:21:04.584
They take the best parts of you,
the human parts,

01:21:04.720 --> 01:21:09.761
and leave only the worst bits,
only the sins.

01:21:09.897 --> 01:21:15.226
I am a bottomless pit of sin.

01:21:15.361 --> 01:21:17.170
(breath trembling)

01:21:17.306 --> 01:21:22.008
What do you think happens
when you die in this realm?

01:21:24.139 --> 01:21:25.671
I'd wake up.

01:21:26.414 --> 01:21:28.271
Maybe.

01:21:28.407 --> 01:21:30.878
Or perhaps...

01:21:31.014 --> 01:21:32.887
you just die.

01:21:36.285 --> 01:21:37.749
It's time to find out.

01:21:39.187 --> 01:21:41.262
(panting rapidly)

01:21:41.397 --> 01:21:43.392
♪ ♪

01:21:54.509 --> 01:21:56.702
(phone ringing)

01:21:58.171 --> 01:21:59.407
Hello?

01:21:59.543 --> 01:22:00.779
FELIX (over phone):
You have to hide.

01:22:00.914 --> 01:22:02.213
(static droning over phone)

01:22:03.981 --> 01:22:06.320
(panting rapidly)

01:22:06.455 --> 01:22:08.648
♪ ♪

01:22:28.136 --> 01:22:29.834
(banging)

01:22:32.580 --> 01:22:34.575
(whimpering)

01:22:39.213 --> 01:22:40.988
(screams)

01:22:46.528 --> 01:22:47.656
Gwen! Gwen!

01:22:47.792 --> 01:22:48.790
Wake up!

01:22:48.925 --> 01:22:49.924
Gwen!

01:22:50.060 --> 01:22:51.497
Gwen, wake up!

01:22:51.633 --> 01:22:53.500
Finn! Mustang!

01:22:53.636 --> 01:22:54.835
FINN:
Gwen.

01:22:54.971 --> 01:22:55.899
MUSTANG:
What's wrong with her?

01:22:56.035 --> 01:22:56.896
FINN:
Gwen. Gwen!

01:22:57.032 --> 01:22:58.599
(yells)

01:23:06.748 --> 01:23:08.708
(breathing heavily)

01:23:11.514 --> 01:23:12.643
MUSTANG (in distance):
Gwen!

01:23:12.779 --> 01:23:14.150
ERNESTO (in distance):
Gwen!

01:23:14.285 --> 01:23:15.814
-Gwen, wake up!
-MUSTANG: Gwen!

01:23:16.823 --> 01:23:18.355
(static crackling)

01:23:27.833 --> 01:23:30.037
♪ ♪

01:23:40.911 --> 01:23:42.212
(grunts)

01:23:42.348 --> 01:23:43.476
-Gwen? Gwen, wake up.
-ERNESTO: Gwen!

01:23:43.611 --> 01:23:44.885
-MUSTANG: Gwen, wake up.
-Gwen!

01:23:45.021 --> 01:23:45.982
-ERNESTO: Gwen, wake up.
-Gwen, wake up!

01:23:46.118 --> 01:23:47.382
-(phone ringing)
-(gasps)

01:23:47.517 --> 01:23:48.812
FINN (in distance):
Gwen, wake up!

01:23:48.948 --> 01:23:50.823
-ERNESTO: Gwen, wake up!
-MUSTANG: Gwen!

01:23:50.958 --> 01:23:52.318
FINN:
Gwen, wake up!

01:23:52.454 --> 01:23:53.617
(phone continues ringing)

01:23:53.753 --> 01:23:56.030
-MUSTANG: Hey!
-ERNESTO: Gwen!

01:23:57.261 --> 01:23:59.660
(phone continues ringing)

01:24:05.340 --> 01:24:08.504
THE GRABBER (over phone):
Ah, naughty girl, Gwen.

01:24:09.406 --> 01:24:11.538
Fuck you with a dinosaur dick.

01:24:11.674 --> 01:24:14.908
Oh, salty tongue
for a girl so young.

01:24:15.044 --> 01:24:16.682
(grunts)

01:24:16.818 --> 01:24:18.680
What are you doing?

01:24:18.816 --> 01:24:20.547
THE GRABBER (over phone):
If someone tries to take

01:24:20.683 --> 01:24:23.947
what power I do have
away from me,

01:24:24.082 --> 01:24:28.420
I have every right
to defend myself.

01:24:28.555 --> 01:24:29.924
(axe thudding on ice)

01:24:30.059 --> 01:24:31.230
Mando.

01:24:32.767 --> 01:24:34.563
(door closing)

01:24:36.337 --> 01:24:38.200
THE GRABBER:
Tell the boys I miss them.

01:24:38.336 --> 01:24:41.031
-(grunts)
-(ice crackling)

01:24:45.041 --> 01:24:46.542
Mando!

01:24:59.422 --> 01:25:00.784
FINN:
Gwen, wake up!

01:25:00.919 --> 01:25:02.294
-(yelps)
-(Mustang grunts)

01:25:05.228 --> 01:25:06.397
(muffled grunting)

01:25:08.101 --> 01:25:10.269
(grunting, panting rapidly)

01:25:14.643 --> 01:25:16.275
(screams)

01:25:20.474 --> 01:25:23.249
(gasping, choking)

01:25:25.383 --> 01:25:26.916
-ERNESTO: Gwen!
-FINN: Gwen!

01:25:27.051 --> 01:25:28.683
(choking)

01:25:29.748 --> 01:25:30.821
(The Grabber grunts)

01:25:30.957 --> 01:25:32.084
(Gwen gasping)

01:25:32.220 --> 01:25:33.259
(grunts)

01:25:41.564 --> 01:25:43.161
-Gwen!
-Keep pressure on it.

01:25:43.297 --> 01:25:44.499
Got it.

01:25:44.635 --> 01:25:46.272
All right,
help me flip her over.

01:25:47.070 --> 01:25:48.966
Gwen.

01:25:49.102 --> 01:25:51.574
FINN (over phone):
Gwen, wake up. Gwen?

01:25:53.081 --> 01:25:54.574
-ERNESTO: Gwen?
-FINN: Okay.

01:25:54.709 --> 01:25:56.277
ERNESTO:
Gwen, can you hear us?

01:25:56.413 --> 01:25:58.143
MUSTANG:
Gwen, wake up.

01:25:58.279 --> 01:25:59.515
-Gwen, wake up!
-Hey, keep pressure
on the wound.

01:25:59.651 --> 01:26:00.911
-Got it.
-Gwen? Gwen, can you hear me?

01:26:01.046 --> 01:26:02.785
-Is she breathing?
-Gwen, come on.

01:26:02.921 --> 01:26:04.621
-You've got to wake up, Gwen.
-Come on. We need help.

01:26:04.756 --> 01:26:05.857
Gwen, Gwen, if you can hear me,
you have to fight back!

01:26:05.992 --> 01:26:08.118
Gwen, fight back!

01:26:12.932 --> 01:26:15.796
(groaning)

01:26:28.809 --> 01:26:30.475
You didn't bring me here.

01:26:30.610 --> 01:26:32.176
I brought myself.

01:26:32.312 --> 01:26:36.355
I chose to come here,
and I can leave when I want.

01:26:37.683 --> 01:26:39.519
I understand now.

01:26:39.655 --> 01:26:42.356
In a dream, I have power, too.

01:26:42.492 --> 01:26:44.264
THE GRABBER:
So?

01:26:45.833 --> 01:26:47.195
(both grunting)

01:26:47.331 --> 01:26:49.396
What are you doing?

01:26:49.531 --> 01:26:51.163
Isn't it obvious?

01:26:51.298 --> 01:26:54.397
I'm fighting back, you grievous,
festering ass wound.

01:26:54.533 --> 01:26:55.473
(yelps)

01:26:59.146 --> 01:27:01.380
See you later, Wild Bill.

01:27:02.510 --> 01:27:03.912
(static crackling)

01:27:04.048 --> 01:27:05.813
(gasps)

01:27:07.821 --> 01:27:09.154
Mando.

01:27:09.289 --> 01:27:11.720
-MUSTANG: Mando!
-(all panting)

01:27:15.490 --> 01:27:18.056
(all grunting)

01:27:21.069 --> 01:27:22.599
ERNESTO:
Is he dead?

01:27:23.598 --> 01:27:24.904
(heavy, shaky breathing)

01:27:25.040 --> 01:27:27.538
I found... I found Felix.

01:27:28.538 --> 01:27:31.278
I found him. I found Felix.

01:27:42.416 --> 01:27:43.618
Mustang?

01:27:43.753 --> 01:27:45.291
-What time is it?
-About 4:30.

01:27:45.426 --> 01:27:46.892
What's happened?
Are you all right?

01:27:47.027 --> 01:27:48.394
Yeah, I'm fine.

01:27:48.529 --> 01:27:50.090
Mando fell through the ice
on Lake Maru.

01:27:50.226 --> 01:27:52.127
Oh, no.

01:27:52.263 --> 01:27:55.665
He's okay, but he found one of
the missing boys in the water.

01:27:57.069 --> 01:27:59.399
We're all gonna start looking
for the other two at dawn.

01:27:59.534 --> 01:28:00.604
We need your help.

01:28:01.772 --> 01:28:03.706
Not with that demon child
out there.

01:28:05.342 --> 01:28:06.808
Her name is Gwen,

01:28:06.943 --> 01:28:09.579
and she is the reason
we got to Mando in time.

01:28:09.715 --> 01:28:12.880
That demon child,
she saved his life.

01:28:13.016 --> 01:28:14.817
-I-I don't know, Mustang. We...
-You know what?

01:28:14.952 --> 01:28:16.785
You want to be all
yellow-bellied and barn-sour,

01:28:16.921 --> 01:28:18.583
lock yourself in this room
until it's safe,

01:28:18.719 --> 01:28:20.593
you go right ahead.

01:28:20.728 --> 01:28:23.330
But that ain't no kind
of true Christian behavior.

01:28:27.926 --> 01:28:29.534
Sun's up at 7:00.

01:28:31.730 --> 01:28:33.934
♪ ♪

01:28:53.787 --> 01:28:55.626
FINN:
Gwen!

01:28:56.625 --> 01:28:58.492
There you are. You okay?

01:28:58.627 --> 01:29:00.994
(vehicle approaching)

01:29:11.675 --> 01:29:13.978
-(Terrence laughs)
-Dad?

01:29:14.113 --> 01:29:15.310
Hey, kids.

01:29:15.446 --> 01:29:16.713
What are you doing here?

01:29:17.949 --> 01:29:20.647
Heard you were snowed in,
so I called in a favor.

01:29:20.782 --> 01:29:22.213
FINN:
Oh, thank God.

01:29:22.349 --> 01:29:23.713
We can finally get you
the hell out of here.

01:29:23.848 --> 01:29:26.225
We have to stay.

01:29:26.360 --> 01:29:27.719
-FINN: What?
-TERRENCE: What?

01:29:27.855 --> 01:29:29.726
GWEN:
We have to stay.

01:29:32.299 --> 01:29:33.495
Wh-What's going on?

01:29:33.631 --> 01:29:35.199
Our work here isn't done.

01:29:35.335 --> 01:29:37.895
He's after her, Dad.

01:29:38.031 --> 01:29:40.539
He's... Who-who's "he?"

01:29:41.634 --> 01:29:42.937
Him.

01:29:45.671 --> 01:29:47.939
(sighs)

01:29:48.074 --> 01:29:50.014
(mutters):
I don't know...

01:29:50.149 --> 01:29:52.342
Gwen, um...

01:29:53.952 --> 01:29:57.347
-Is this more dream stuff?
-FINN: Dad, don't.

01:30:00.053 --> 01:30:01.693
Okay, we're getting out of here.

01:30:01.828 --> 01:30:04.162
-Come on. Let's go.
-I'll get my stuff.

01:30:04.298 --> 01:30:05.927
I'm not going anywhere.

01:30:07.297 --> 01:30:08.325
Gwen.

01:30:09.798 --> 01:30:11.171
He's going to kill you.

01:30:11.306 --> 01:30:13.402
Okay, and I can't stop him.

01:30:13.537 --> 01:30:14.902
But we have a chance.

01:30:15.038 --> 01:30:16.574
A chance to protect you,
to keep you safe.

01:30:16.710 --> 01:30:18.444
You're gonna take care
of me, Finn?

01:30:18.579 --> 01:30:21.539
You can't even take care
of yourself.

01:30:21.675 --> 01:30:24.141
You are just like fucking Dad,
putting your head in the sand

01:30:24.277 --> 01:30:25.917
and numbing yourself
into oblivion.

01:30:26.052 --> 01:30:27.277
Whoa.

01:30:27.413 --> 01:30:28.818
(chuckling):
Where did that come from?

01:30:28.953 --> 01:30:30.122
You've seen
what he's been doing.

01:30:30.258 --> 01:30:31.955
You're just ignoring it,

01:30:32.091 --> 01:30:33.819
pretending you don't
smell it on him, in his room,

01:30:33.954 --> 01:30:34.951
-in the backyard.
-Narc.

01:30:35.087 --> 01:30:36.395
You can't narc about

01:30:36.531 --> 01:30:38.126
what everyone already knows,
dingus.

01:30:38.261 --> 01:30:40.399
You're just smoking your
fucking life away to pretend

01:30:40.534 --> 01:30:41.462
-none of this happened.
-Shut up.

01:30:41.598 --> 01:30:42.996
Well, it happened, Finn.

01:30:43.132 --> 01:30:44.733
-Shut up.
-And it happened to those kids.

01:30:44.869 --> 01:30:46.563
-Shut up.
-And it's happening now.

01:30:46.699 --> 01:30:47.965
And you two just want to run
and hide like you always do.

01:30:48.101 --> 01:30:49.332
-Shut up.
-Bottle, joint.

01:30:49.468 --> 01:30:50.971
-Same fucking Friday night.
-Shut up!

01:30:51.107 --> 01:30:52.910
-Anything to stop the pain.
-Shut up!

01:30:53.046 --> 01:30:54.976
Anything to feel for a few hours
like what happened to you

01:30:55.111 --> 01:30:57.079
down in that basement
wasn't real!

01:30:57.215 --> 01:30:58.951
Shut up!

01:30:59.086 --> 01:31:01.411
All right, you don't think
I don't know it was real?

01:31:02.889 --> 01:31:05.723
You think I don't fucking know
it was real?

01:31:07.956 --> 01:31:10.156
It's all I ever think about.

01:31:11.365 --> 01:31:12.830
All right, you don't...

01:31:12.965 --> 01:31:14.331
you don't know
what it was like down there.

01:31:14.466 --> 01:31:16.063
Nobody fucking knows.

01:31:19.438 --> 01:31:21.231
All right, I was...

01:31:21.366 --> 01:31:24.742
(sobbing):
I was so fucking scared.

01:31:30.743 --> 01:31:32.143
(groans)

01:31:32.279 --> 01:31:35.181
God, I don't want to be
angry anymore.

01:31:37.324 --> 01:31:39.284
(continues sobbing)

01:31:51.430 --> 01:31:54.068
I don't want to be
afraid anymore.

01:31:58.573 --> 01:32:00.107
Hey.

01:32:03.145 --> 01:32:05.552
You're the bravest person
I know.

01:32:06.617 --> 01:32:09.182
(breathing heavily)

01:32:12.653 --> 01:32:14.056
Okay.

01:32:14.192 --> 01:32:16.563
Gwen, look at me, please.
I know you want to stay.

01:32:16.698 --> 01:32:19.562
I know, but if you really are
in danger here,

01:32:19.697 --> 01:32:22.002
we need to leave right now.

01:32:22.137 --> 01:32:24.495
-No.
-(sighs)

01:32:24.631 --> 01:32:28.598
Sweetheart, I'm sorry,
but I'm not asking.

01:32:28.733 --> 01:32:30.842
What are you gonna do, Dad?
You gonna beat me?

01:32:30.977 --> 01:32:33.035
Take off your belt
and whip me into the truck?

01:32:33.171 --> 01:32:34.238
Don't, don't...

01:32:34.374 --> 01:32:36.540
Go ahead and try.
See if it works.

01:32:36.676 --> 01:32:38.076
Your mother, right there.
There's your mother.

01:32:38.211 --> 01:32:40.379
You're just like your mother.

01:32:40.515 --> 01:32:43.223
Stubborn! You're so stubborn
right to the end,

01:32:43.358 --> 01:32:45.058
even in the face of reality.

01:32:45.193 --> 01:32:46.954
The end? The end?

01:32:47.090 --> 01:32:49.024
Let me tell you
about the end, Dad.

01:32:50.057 --> 01:32:52.258
Mom didn't kill herself.

01:32:54.730 --> 01:32:56.097
Okay. That's it.

01:32:56.232 --> 01:32:57.928
Let's all get
in the goddamn truck.

01:32:58.064 --> 01:33:00.339
No, no, wait, Gwen.

01:33:00.474 --> 01:33:02.268
What are you talking about?

01:33:03.574 --> 01:33:05.372
Mom's dreams.

01:33:05.507 --> 01:33:08.679
She was dreaming about
a missing kid, wasn't she?

01:33:08.814 --> 01:33:10.881
Talking about camp
before she died.

01:33:11.016 --> 01:33:12.251
That's why you remembered
the camp.

01:33:12.387 --> 01:33:14.379
Yeah, but... Yeah, so? So?

01:33:14.514 --> 01:33:17.557
She found him
long before he took Finn,

01:33:17.693 --> 01:33:21.122
and he saw her,
and he came to our house.

01:33:22.756 --> 01:33:23.927
No.

01:33:25.595 --> 01:33:27.700
Holy shit.

01:33:28.700 --> 01:33:31.464
He showed me that he killed her.

01:33:31.600 --> 01:33:35.004
Dad, what was the first thing
you said when you saw Mom?

01:33:36.539 --> 01:33:37.835
What?

01:33:37.971 --> 01:33:39.744
You asked her,

01:33:39.879 --> 01:33:42.808
"What did you do?
What did you do?"

01:33:42.944 --> 01:33:45.345
And you blamed yourself.

01:33:45.481 --> 01:33:48.919
-You said, "What have I done?"
-(breathing heavily)

01:33:51.090 --> 01:33:54.791
We were asleep when it happened,
when you found her.

01:33:54.927 --> 01:33:56.960
How else could I know
what you said?

01:33:58.093 --> 01:34:00.198
It wasn't your fault, Dad.

01:34:00.333 --> 01:34:02.502
Oh, my God.

01:34:02.637 --> 01:34:04.103
GWEN:
And it wasn't hers.

01:34:04.238 --> 01:34:05.661
Oh, my God.

01:34:05.797 --> 01:34:09.132
The man who took Finn
took her away from us

01:34:09.268 --> 01:34:11.073
because she was onto him.

01:34:13.474 --> 01:34:15.946
Because her dreams
weren't just dreams.

01:34:19.244 --> 01:34:21.083
And neither are mine.

01:34:30.330 --> 01:34:32.523
♪ ♪

01:34:35.330 --> 01:34:37.627
MANDO:
All right, pass me the cable.

01:34:48.616 --> 01:34:50.684
GWEN:
<i> Hey, Jesus.</i>

01:34:51.717 --> 01:34:53.687
<i> I'm not doing so well.</i>

01:34:54.520 --> 01:34:56.080
<i> I need help.</i>

01:34:56.216 --> 01:34:57.988
<i> Some real fucking help.</i>

01:34:59.685 --> 01:35:02.086
<i> We got to find</i>
<i> those other two boys</i>

01:35:02.222 --> 01:35:04.564
<i> to take away his power.</i>

01:35:04.699 --> 01:35:07.030
<i> I'm scared he's gonna kill me.</i>

01:35:08.030 --> 01:35:10.130
<i> For real this time.</i>

01:35:10.265 --> 01:35:12.471
<i> Please don't let that happen.</i>

01:35:12.607 --> 01:35:13.905
<i> Get us out of here alive.</i>

01:35:15.510 --> 01:35:17.469
<i> Don't let him win.</i>

01:35:18.278 --> 01:35:19.974
(sighs)

01:35:20.109 --> 01:35:21.539
We're pretty much out of light.

01:35:22.851 --> 01:35:25.550
Maybe Spike and Cal
are down too deep.

01:35:25.686 --> 01:35:27.180
I was thinking the same thing.

01:35:27.315 --> 01:35:28.821
We should've seen 'em by now.

01:35:28.956 --> 01:35:31.157
(conversation continues quietly
in distance)

01:35:31.292 --> 01:35:33.485
♪ ♪

01:35:48.342 --> 01:35:50.268
Hey, whoa, girl.

01:35:50.403 --> 01:35:52.240
You've done enough for today.

01:35:59.519 --> 01:36:01.381
(static crackles)

01:36:06.025 --> 01:36:07.618
MUSTANG (muffled):
Oh, no, Gwen.

01:36:08.724 --> 01:36:10.262
Gwen!

01:36:10.398 --> 01:36:12.022
Gwen, wake up.

01:36:12.157 --> 01:36:13.426
Need some help!

01:36:15.435 --> 01:36:16.902
(panting)

01:36:24.169 --> 01:36:25.574
Hey, Gwen.

01:36:25.710 --> 01:36:27.040
Gwen, wake up.

01:36:27.175 --> 01:36:29.745
Sh-She accidentally fell asleep.

01:36:29.880 --> 01:36:31.580
Accidentally, my ass.

01:36:31.715 --> 01:36:34.315
♪ ♪

01:36:51.669 --> 01:36:53.873
♪ ♪

01:37:05.484 --> 01:37:07.711
(yells)

01:37:09.756 --> 01:37:11.682
(Kenneth continues yelling)

01:37:17.894 --> 01:37:19.657
He's here.

01:37:27.465 --> 01:37:30.173
(yelling continues)

01:37:33.647 --> 01:37:35.541
(Barbara whimpering)

01:37:46.493 --> 01:37:48.752
♪ ♪

01:37:53.559 --> 01:37:55.031
-(whooshing)
-(both groan)

01:37:55.167 --> 01:37:57.761
MUSTANG:
Oh, my God. Ken, Barbara!

01:38:06.641 --> 01:38:09.012
FINN:
He's still here. Keep looking.

01:38:09.148 --> 01:38:11.882
MANDO:
Where is he? Where did he go?

01:38:12.017 --> 01:38:13.678
ERNESTO:
The ice is breaking!

01:38:16.985 --> 01:38:18.584
The cable!

01:38:31.837 --> 01:38:34.204
(breathing heavily)

01:38:35.202 --> 01:38:37.009
(scraping on ice)

01:38:38.071 --> 01:38:39.946
Finn!

01:38:43.551 --> 01:38:45.545
Whoa! (groans)

01:38:46.545 --> 01:38:48.418
How the tables have turned.

01:38:48.553 --> 01:38:50.616
-(choking)
-(The Grabber grunts
aggressively)

01:38:53.025 --> 01:38:56.457
Ernesto, get her out of here.

01:39:06.601 --> 01:39:08.337
THE GRABBER:
I remember the feeling.

01:39:09.369 --> 01:39:11.604
Breathless, scared,

01:39:11.740 --> 01:39:14.610
the whole of the world
starting to fade away.

01:39:14.746 --> 01:39:16.543
ERNESTO: I've got Gwen.
Watch out. I'm coming through.

01:39:16.679 --> 01:39:18.545
-MANDO: You all right?
-MUSTANG: Here. Here.

01:39:25.786 --> 01:39:28.093
-MUSTANG: You got him?
-Yeah. I got him.

01:39:30.465 --> 01:39:32.163
(grunting)

01:39:38.233 --> 01:39:40.435
(grunting, panting)

01:39:43.071 --> 01:39:45.605
(straining)

01:39:56.580 --> 01:39:58.387
(static crackling)

01:39:59.486 --> 01:40:03.652
"O grave, where is thy victory?

01:40:03.788 --> 01:40:07.000
O death, where is thy sting?"

01:40:11.631 --> 01:40:14.073
THE GRABBER:
Scripture?

01:40:15.973 --> 01:40:18.038
God's not here.

01:40:18.173 --> 01:40:19.639
You're alone.

01:40:21.647 --> 01:40:22.977
No.

01:40:23.112 --> 01:40:24.644
I brought friends.

01:40:32.419 --> 01:40:35.622
(gruff, heavy breathing)

01:40:58.982 --> 01:41:01.780
♪ ♪

01:41:11.896 --> 01:41:13.693
(both grunt)

01:41:18.872 --> 01:41:21.168
The boys are found.

01:41:21.303 --> 01:41:22.742
You're powerless.

01:41:22.877 --> 01:41:25.072
(The Grabber breathing heavily)

01:41:25.207 --> 01:41:27.839
(pained squealing)

01:41:30.478 --> 01:41:33.515
(grunting, panting frantically)

01:41:50.234 --> 01:41:52.435
Oh, you're so fucked.

01:41:53.468 --> 01:41:55.673
Hell isn't flames, Bill.

01:41:55.809 --> 01:41:57.434
It's ice.

01:41:57.570 --> 01:42:00.344
(grunting fiercely)

01:42:07.251 --> 01:42:09.012
You don't scare me.

01:42:19.629 --> 01:42:22.729
-(Gwen grunting)
-(pained squealing)

01:42:30.975 --> 01:42:32.673
(splashing)

01:42:48.223 --> 01:42:50.691
(panting)

01:42:53.360 --> 01:42:55.564
♪ ♪

01:42:59.300 --> 01:43:01.570
(burbling)

01:43:04.844 --> 01:43:07.037
♪ ♪

01:43:10.784 --> 01:43:13.648
(ice crackling)

01:43:28.526 --> 01:43:30.031
Hey.

01:43:30.166 --> 01:43:31.864
You okay?

01:43:33.532 --> 01:43:35.736
♪ ♪

01:43:46.846 --> 01:43:48.485
FINN:
You did good, Dad.

01:43:53.127 --> 01:43:54.452
GWEN:
It's over.

01:43:54.587 --> 01:43:56.556
He's gone.

01:43:56.691 --> 01:43:58.430
FINN:
Where'd he go?

01:43:58.565 --> 01:44:01.300
GWEN: The boys took him back
to where he belongs.

01:44:12.403 --> 01:44:15.611
Hi. This is Armando Reyes
from Alpine Lake.

01:44:18.246 --> 01:44:19.411
Yeah.

01:44:19.546 --> 01:44:20.811
Good, good. Yeah.

01:44:20.947 --> 01:44:23.256
I know it's-it's been a minute.

01:44:24.224 --> 01:44:27.058
The reason why I'm calling is

01:44:27.194 --> 01:44:29.592
I have some news about Calvin.

01:44:31.259 --> 01:44:32.760
Yes.

01:44:34.761 --> 01:44:37.699
Yeah, we finally found him.

01:44:43.503 --> 01:44:45.707
(phone ringing)

01:44:47.407 --> 01:44:49.205
What?

01:44:50.348 --> 01:44:52.208
You can't hear that?

01:44:53.418 --> 01:44:55.414
-Uh-uh.
-The phone is ringing.

01:44:55.550 --> 01:44:57.785
(ringing continues)

01:45:00.093 --> 01:45:01.684
Must be for you, then.

01:45:01.820 --> 01:45:04.088
(ringing continues)

01:45:19.078 --> 01:45:21.837
(static crackling)

01:45:21.973 --> 01:45:24.315
(voice shaking):
Hello?

01:45:24.450 --> 01:45:26.345
HOPE (over phone):
Hi, sweetie.

01:45:26.480 --> 01:45:28.684
♪ ♪

01:45:31.258 --> 01:45:34.184
-Mom?
-Mm-hmm. Yeah, baby.

01:45:34.319 --> 01:45:36.989
I don't have much time,
but it's me.

01:45:38.660 --> 01:45:40.799
(sniffles, breathes shakily)

01:45:40.935 --> 01:45:43.296
Where are you?

01:45:43.431 --> 01:45:45.036
You know where.

01:45:45.172 --> 01:45:46.803
It's beautiful here.

01:45:46.939 --> 01:45:49.171
(crying)

01:45:49.306 --> 01:45:51.635
-It is?
-Mm.

01:45:51.771 --> 01:45:54.171
Yeah, so beautiful.

01:45:55.345 --> 01:45:56.782
Just like you.

01:45:56.917 --> 01:45:58.549
(sniffles)

01:46:00.813 --> 01:46:03.517
I... I miss you, Mom.

01:46:03.653 --> 01:46:06.986
Oh. I miss you, too, sweetie.

01:46:08.359 --> 01:46:10.259
But you did so well.

01:46:10.394 --> 01:46:12.530
You saved those boys.

01:46:14.733 --> 01:46:17.832
-I didn't save anyone.
-Yes, you did.

01:46:18.698 --> 01:46:20.065
You set them free.

01:46:20.200 --> 01:46:22.507
They're here
where they belong now.

01:46:23.503 --> 01:46:25.110
Wait.

01:46:25.245 --> 01:46:27.413
I have to ask you something.

01:46:28.542 --> 01:46:30.746
Ask me anything.

01:46:36.455 --> 01:46:39.392
Will I always be this cursed?

01:46:40.960 --> 01:46:42.428
Oh.

01:46:43.725 --> 01:46:45.992
It's not a curse, baby.

01:46:47.332 --> 01:46:49.567
It was never a curse.

01:46:52.798 --> 01:46:54.737
I have to go.

01:46:55.671 --> 01:46:59.036
Tell your brother I love him

01:46:59.171 --> 01:47:02.371
-and that Robin says hi.
-(sobbing)

01:47:07.386 --> 01:47:09.653
(static droning over phone)

01:47:17.790 --> 01:47:19.630
(static stops)

01:47:28.437 --> 01:47:30.641
♪ ♪

01:47:42.947 --> 01:47:45.920
(voice muted)

01:48:03.934 --> 01:48:06.138
♪ ♪

01:48:09.745 --> 01:48:10.978
TERRENCE:
Kids!

01:48:12.019 --> 01:48:13.314
Time to go.

01:48:13.450 --> 01:48:14.949
Get a move on.

01:48:26.261 --> 01:48:28.791
TERRENCE: So, what do you think
of that Ernesto boy?

01:48:28.926 --> 01:48:30.028
(engine starts)

01:48:30.164 --> 01:48:32.329
FINN:
She could do a lot worse.

01:48:32.465 --> 01:48:34.465
-TERRENCE: How about you?
-FINN: No, Dad...

01:48:34.601 --> 01:48:36.674
TERRENCE: That Mustang girl
seemed pretty cute to me.

01:48:36.809 --> 01:48:39.776
FINN: Ah. Dad, please just...
just drive.

01:48:40.909 --> 01:48:43.007
TERRENCE:
Just saying.

01:48:43.142 --> 01:48:44.847
FINN:
Eyes on the road.

01:48:44.982 --> 01:48:47.216
TERRENCE:
All right, I'm just saying.

01:48:47.351 --> 01:48:49.555
♪ ♪

